t["npc:menara-voidrender"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,347,19.503.0,19.441.0,17.416.1,25.230.0,45.276.0,45.232.0,39.275.0,44.214.0,42.202.0",["h"]="0a1d74",["n"]="Menara Nadiz",["s"]="Menara Nadiz. Menara Nadiz es una bruja humana que reside en el puerto goblin de Trinquete. Actúa como mentora para ambiciosos practicantes de las artes oscuras procedentes tanto de la Alianza como de la Horda, compartiendo sus profundos conocimientos sobre artefactos de atadura demoníaca y artesanía arcana. Su posición aislada en Kalimdor la mantiene lejos de la atenta mirada de las autoridades ortodoxas. Mientras la mayoría de los brujos de los Reinos del Este practican en sótanos húmedos o en mataderos apartados bajo sus ciudades de origen, Menara Nadiz eligió el neutral puerto goblin de Trinquete, en Los Baldíos. Al operar lejos del escrutinio del Kirin Tor, de los guardias de Ventormenta o de los capataces de Orgrimmar, es libre de dedicarse a sus estudios ocultistas a la vista de todos. Su disposición a tratar con cualquier aprendiz capaz, sin importar su facción, la convierte en un insólito punto de encuentro entre los practicantes de las artes oscuras.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warlock"]="Menara is a vital mentor on Kalimdor, teaching practitioners from both factions how to forge their signature enchanted robes and bind demons into focus orbs.",["profession:Tailoring"]="Menara blends advanced tailoring materials with fel reagents to weave durable, spell-woven vestments capable of channeling demonic power.",["race:Human"]="Far from Stormwind's catacombs, Menara represents human warlocks who cast aside kingdom loyalties to pursue dark arts unhindered in neutral territories."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Menara Voidrender is a human warlock stationed in the neutral port town of Ratchet in the Barrens. She serves as an instructor and artificer for developing warlocks, guiding them through crafting rituals and demon-binding sorcery.",["al"]={"who is menara","menara voidrender lore","who is the warlock in ratchet"},["q"]="Who is Menara Voidrender?"},{["a"]="Ratchet offers neutrality and distance from the watchful eyes of major governments. By basing herself in a goblin-run port, Menara can practice forbidden arts and instruct students from both the Alliance and the Horde without interference from paladins, mages, or city guards.",["al"]={"why is menara in ratchet","why is she in the barrens","why ratchet warlock"},["q"]="Why is a human warlock living in the Barrens?"},{["a"]="Menara specializes in demonology, enchanting dark fabrics, and fashioning vessels designed to trap demonic entities. She is especially known for her mastery in creating and restoring orbs that bind demons, such as the Orb of Orahil.",["al"]={"what does menara teach","menara voidrender powers","what is menara good at"},["q"]="What kind of magic does Menara specialize in?"},{["a"]="Menara and the reclusive sorceress Tabetha share a past connection. Despite Tabetha living secluded in Dustwallow Marsh and practicing traditional wizardry, warlocks seeking knowledge regarding the Orb of Orahil find that the two women are familiar with each other's talents.",["al"]={"menara and tabetha","how does she know tabetha","tabetha connection"},["q"]="What is Menara's connection to Tabetha?"},{["a"]="Menara operates neutrally out of Ratchet. She offers her tutelage and crafting tasks to any warlock who proves competent and ambitious enough to handle fel energies, welcoming both Alliance and Horde practitioners.",["al"]={"is menara alliance or horde","menara faction","who does menara work for"},["q"]="Does Menara favor the Alliance or the Horde?"},{["a"]="Menara directs apprentices in weaving the Enchanted Gold Bloodrobe, a garment imbued with demonic power, and assists advanced practitioners in recovering and assembling components for the Orb of Orahil.",["al"]={"menara quests","what does she make","enchanted gold bloodrobe menara"},["q"]="What major artifacts does she help create?"}},["kw"]={"barrens","bloodrobe","demonology","menara","orahil","ratchet","tabetha","voidrender","warlock"},["n"]="Menara Voidrender",["s"]="Menara Voidrender is a human warlock residing in the goblin port of Ratchet. She acts as a mentor to ambitious practitioners of the dark arts from both the Alliance and the Horde, sharing her deep knowledge of demon-binding artifacts and arcane craft. Her secluded position in Kalimdor keeps her far from the watchful eyes of orthodox authorities.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While most warlocks in the Eastern Kingdoms practice in damp cellars or secluded slaughterhouses beneath their home cities, Menara Voidrender chose the neutral goblin port of Ratchet in the Barrens. Operating far from the scrutiny of the Kirin Tor, Stormwind's guards, or Orgrimmar's overseers, she is free to pursue her occult studies in plain sight. Her willingness to deal with any capable apprentice, regardless of faction, makes her a rare point of commonality among practitioners of the dark arts.",["t"]="A Refuge in Ratchet"},{["b"]="Menara is renowned among veteran conjurers as an authority on creating orbs that imprison and harness demonic spirits. She works closely with intricate reagents, guiding apprentices through demanding rituals to forge enchanted attire and binding implements. Word of her expertise reaches as far as Ironforge and the Undercity, leading senior warlocks across Azeroth to direct their most promising students across the sea to seek her counsel.",["t"]="Mistress of Binding"},{["b"]="Among Menara's distant acquaintances is the hermit mage Tabetha, who lives in deep isolation in the swamps of Dustwallow Marsh. Though Tabetha pursues the arcane and Menara delves into fel bindings and demonology, the two women share an old history. When powerful relics like the Orb of Orahil require restoration or specialized knowledge, their shared past becomes an unexpected bridge across Kalimdor's wilderness.",["t"]="Ties to the Marsh"}}}}}
t["npc:miner-johnson"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,379,23.446.0,30.398.0,21.192.0,39.225.0,37.202.0,35.170.0,46.198.0,52.221.0",["h"]="904b87",["n"]="Minero Johnson",["s"]="Minero Johnson. El Minero Johnson es un minero esquivo y curtido, afiliado a la Hermandad Defias en lo más profundo de Las Minas de la Muerte. Oculto en una alcoba lateral junto a peones comunes, este peligroso prospector supervisa las labores de excavación antes de llegar a la maquinaria pesada de las profundidades subterráneas. Como vaga de manera impredecible por los túneles subterráneos, los aventureros solo se cruzan con él en contadas ocasiones. Mientras cientos de trabajadores pican las vetas subterráneas de Las Minas de la Muerte para abastecer la fortaleza oculta de Edwin VanCleef, el Minero Johnson destaca entre ellos como una figura inusualmente formidable. Acechando en una sombría alcoba a la izquierda antes de los pesados trituradores de la Sala de los Mástiles, es mucho más resistente y agresivo que la plantilla habitual. Su impredecible presencia lo convierte en un objetivo legendario para los exploradores que atraviesan los túneles Defias.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Striking down Johnson disrupts the steady stream of smeltable ore flowing into the Defias war machine hidden below Moonbrook.",["profession:Mining"]="For prospectors, Johnson represents the rugged, lawless side of subterranean labor, guarding rich mineral deposits deep beneath Westfall with blood and pickaxe."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Miner Johnson is a rare elite human miner allied with the Defias Brotherhood. He works deep within the Deadmines, situated in a side alcove with other laborers just before the goblin shredder.",["al"]={"miner johnson lore","who is miner johnson","deadmines miner johnson"},["q"]="Who is Miner Johnson?"},{["a"]="He can be found in the upper shafts of the Deadmines before reaching the room housing Sneed and his shredder. Look for a small excavation alcove off to the left where a pocket of miners are actively chipping away at the rock.",["al"]={"miner johnson location","where is miner johnson","how to find miner johnson"},["q"]="Where exactly is Miner Johnson located?"},{["a"]="Miner Johnson is a rare spawn, meaning he only appears occasionally when an expedition enters the Deadmines. Most groups running through the mine shafts will find an ordinary miner in his place instead.",["al"]={"miner johnson not spawning","is miner johnson rare","miner johnson spawn rate"},["q"]="Why isn't Miner Johnson always there?"},{["a"]="Miner Johnson is not associated with any formal quest bounty. He is simply an opportunistic encounter for dungeon delve parties lucky enough to find him working the seam.",["al"]={"miner johnson quest","does miner johnson have a quest"},["q"]="Is Miner Johnson part of any quest?"},{["a"]="He is an experienced foreman or master digger helping the Defias Brotherhood extract precious metal, stone, and resources necessary to construct their massive underground base and hidden juggernaut.",["al"]={"what does miner johnson do","miner johnson role"},["q"]="What is Miner Johnson's role in the Deadmines?"},{["a"]="Yes. While the standard diggers throughout the Deadmines are relatively fragile, Miner Johnson is an elite combatant with significantly more vitality and striking power, requiring a coordinated group to bring down safely.",["al"]={"how hard is miner johnson","is miner johnson elite"},["q"]="Is Miner Johnson dangerous compared to other miners?"}},["kw"]={"alcove","deadmines","defias","elite","miner johnson","moonbrook","rare","shredder","westfall"},["n"]="Miner Johnson",["s"]="Miner Johnson is an elusive, seasoned miner affiliated with the Defias Brotherhood deep inside the Deadmines. Tucked away in a side alcove alongside ordinary laborers, this dangerous prospector oversees excavation efforts ahead of the heavy machinery found deeper underground. Because he wanders the subterranean tunnels erratically, adventurers only occasionally cross his path.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While hundreds of laborers pick at the subterranean veins of the Deadmines to supply Edwin VanCleef's hidden fortress, Miner Johnson stands out as an unusually formidable figure among them. Lurking in a shadowed alcove to the left before the lumbering shredders of the Mast Room, he is far tougher and more aggressive than the regular workforce. His unpredictable presence makes him a legendary target for explorers traversing the Defias tunnels.",["t"]="A Rare Face in the Deep"},{["b"]="The Defias Brotherhood's clandestine operation beneath Moonbrook requires vast amounts of raw ore to forge weapons, reinforce shafts, and assemble mechanical contraptions. Miners like Johnson provide the muscle behind the metal, hacking away at the rich mineral seams beneath Westfall. Anyone stumbling into Johnson's workspace will quickly discover that he defends his dig site with lethal fervor.",["t"]="Fueling the Defias War Machine"}}}}}
t["npc:motega-firemane"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,267,22.511.0,20.632.1,22.483.1,23.204.0,35.153.0,38.275.1,56.248.1,44.276.1,45.212.0",["h"]="646772",["n"]="Motega Pirocabello",["s"]="Motega Pirocabello. Motega Pirocabello es un erudito tauren apostado en el Campamento del Tramo Blanco en Las Mil Agujas. Dedicado a catalogar la peligrosa fauna del cañón, ve interrumpidos sus estudios por el espíritu vengativo de una serpiente alada y las temerarias desventuras de su joven ayudante. Cuatro años después de la Tercera Guerra, Motega Pirocabello viajó hacia el sur, a Las Mil Agujas, para observar y registrar a las singulares bestias que sobrevivían entre las imponentes mesetas. Acompañado por su joven ayudante, Pao'ka Velocimontés —cuyo protector padre se resistía a dejarlo marchar de Mulgore—, Motega montó un campamento junto a Kanati Nubegris en el Campamento del Tramo Blanco. Aunque su vocación original era la tranquila observación natural, los duros peligros del fondo del cañón exigen constantemente un enfoque más marcial para sobrevivir.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,1,1,1,0},["sec"]={0,1,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Hunter"]="Hunters find common ground with Motega, who relies on skilled trackers to harvest canyon flora, track wyverns in Highperch, and stalk the mighty spirit Arikara.",["faction:Horde"]="Motega represents the Horde's expansion into the untamed regions of Kalimdor, maintaining a tenuous research outpost while safeguarding High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof from spiritual threats.",["race:Tauren"]="Through his reverence for nature and dutiful devotion to Cairne Bloodhoof, Motega embodies the tauren ethos of studying the Earth Mother's creatures while defending the tribe against ancient spirits."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Motega Firemane is a tauren researcher stationed at Whitereach Post in Thousand Needles. He came to the canyons to study the local wildlife alongside fellow braves and his assistant, Pao'ka Swiftmountain.",["al"]={"motega firemane lore","who is motega","whitereach motega"},["q"]="Who is Motega Firemane?"},{["a"]="He is located at Whitereach Post, a small Horde campsite nestled along the canyon floor of Thousand Needles, situated north of the shimmering salt flats.",["al"]={"motega location","where is motega firemane","motega firemane map"},["q"]="Where can Motega Firemane be found?"},{["a"]="Arikara is a vengeful serpent spirit that has manifested in Thousand Needles targeting Cairne Bloodhoof. Though baffled as to why the spirit bears a grudge against the High Chieftain, Motega takes the threat seriously and directs hunters to summon and eliminate the creature.",["al"]={"who is arikara","why kill arikara","arikara cairne"},["q"]="Why is Motega concerned about Arikara?"},{["a"]="Motega tasks adventurers with collecting Incendia agave and carrying it to Magatha Grimtotem on the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff. Magatha uses her shamanic knowledge to enchant the plant into a sacred powder capable of summoning the elusive Arikara.",["al"]={"magatha incendia powder","motega and magatha","sacred fire quest lore"},["q"]="What role does Magatha Grimtotem play in Motega's plans?"},{["a"]="Pao'ka Swiftmountain strayed into the dangerous wyvern roosts of Highperch and became lost. Motega was anxious over the youth's fate, especially given how reluctant Pao'ka's father had been to allow the journey, but travelers successfully escorted him back to Whitereach Post.",["al"]={"pao'ka swiftmountain","missing tauren highperch","homeward bound quest"},["q"]="What happened to Motega's companion, Pao'ka?"},{["a"]="Beyond rogue spirits and predators, the camp is actively targeted by the nearby Galak centaur, who orchestrate ambushes and plot assassinations against Kanati Greycloud and the other tauren stationed at the post.",["al"]={"whitereach post threats","centaur at whitereach","galak centaur plot"},["q"]="What other dangers does Whitereach Post face?"}},["kw"]={"arikara","cairne bloodhoof","kanati greycloud","magatha grimtotem","motega firemane","pao'ka swiftmountain","thousand needles","whitereach post"},["n"]="Motega Firemane",["s"]="Motega Firemane is a tauren scholar stationed at Whitereach Post in Thousand Needles. Dedicated to cataloging the dangerous wildlife of the canyon, he finds his studies disrupted by a vengeful wind serpent spirit and the reckless misadventures of his young assistant.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Four years following the Third War, Motega Firemane journeyed south into Thousand Needles to observe and record the distinct beasts surviving among the towering mesas. Accompanied by his youthful assistant, Pao'ka Swiftmountain—whose protective father was reluctant to let him leave Mulgore—Motega set up camp alongside Kanati Greycloud at Whitereach Post. While his original calling was quiet natural observation, the harsh perils of the canyon floor continually demand a more martial approach to survival.",["t"]="Scholar of the Canyons"},{["b"]="Motega's peaceful research was upended when word arrived from Freewind Post that Arikara, a ferocious and legendary winged serpent spirit, had returned to the canyons seeking vengeance against Cairne Bloodhoof. Perplexed by why such a creature held a vendetta against the High Chieftain, Motega acted swiftly to protect the Horde. He instructed scouts to gather Incendia agave from the canyon basin and carry it to Elder Magatha Grimtotem in Thunder Bluff to be enchanted into a sacred powder. Using this preparation, hunters summoned and slew the serpent spirit, returning its hide to Whitereach Post as proof that Cairne was safe.",["t"]="The Wrath of Arikara"},{["b"]="Arikara was not the only hazard challenging Motega's stay at Whitereach Post. Local Galak centaur continuously probed the camp, even scheming an assassination plot against Kanati Greycloud and his followers. To worsen matters, young Pao'ka wandered away from the safety of the campfire and vanished into the wyvern-infested heights of Highperch. Though frustrated by the young brave's thoughtlessness, Motega was immensely relieved when Horde travelers escorted the youth back alive.",["t"]="Guardian of Whitereach"}}}}}
t["npc:mr-smite"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="9,349,22.480.0,21.512.0,55.342.0,28.219.0,49.205.0,29.166.0,27.133.0,52.214.0",["h"]="43383e",["n"]="Don Mamporro",["s"]="Don Mamporro. Don Mamporro es el imponente tauren y primer oficial que sirve a bordo del buque insignia de la Hermandad Defias en las profundidades de Las Minas de la Muerte. Experto maestro de armas a las órdenes del Capitán Verdetez, vigila el acceso del muelle hacia el gigante oculto con una disciplina implacable. Los intrusos que se enfrentan a él deben lidiar con su arsenal cambiante y su demoledora fuerza física. Al custodiar los muelles de la Cala del Acorazado, Don Mamporro ejerce como primer oficial del goblin Capitán Verdetez. Si bien la Hermandad Defias está compuesta predominantemente por humanos descontentos y manitas goblin aliados, Don Mamporro destaca como una sorprendente anomalía: un tauren gigantesco y curtido en combate, muy lejos de las llanuras de Kalimdor. Encargado de mantener un orden férreo entre una tripulación pirata alborotadora, se asegura de que los trabajos de preparación del acorazado secreto de Edwin VanCleef prosigan sin interrupciones.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warrior"]="Smite demonstrates remarkable martial discipline, seamlessly transitioning between swift single-handed strikes, dual-wielded axes, and punishing two-handed hammer blows.",["faction:Alliance"]="Smite serves as the primary barrier preventing Alliance agents from storming the gangplank to reach Captain Greenskin and Edwin VanCleef.",["race:Tauren"]="Seeing a fellow tauren serving as a cutthroat first mate among seafaring outlaws in the Eastern Kingdoms is a jarring sight for any traveler from Mulgore."},["faq"]={{["a"]="While the vast majority of tauren dwell in Kalimdor alongside their Horde allies, mercenary outcasts and wanderers occasionally find their way east. Smite serves as a pirate officer rather than an ideological follower of the Defias Brotherhood, hired alongside Captain Greenskin's crew to supervise the cove and ready the dreadnaught for sea.",["al"]={"why tauren in deadmines","mr smite lore","tauren pirate"},["q"]="Why is a tauren working with human bandits in Westfall?"},{["a"]="Smite answers directly to Captain Greenskin, the goblin master of the pirate vessel anchored in Ironclad Cove. Above them both in the overall conspiracy stands Edwin VanCleef, the grand leader of the Defias Brotherhood.",["al"]={"who is smite's boss","who does mr smite work for"},["q"]="Who is Mr. Smite's superior?"},{["a"]="Smite begins battle with a Thief's Blade. As the fight turns against him, he retreats to his chest to equip a pair of Smite's Reavers, and finally draws out Smite's Mighty Hammer when pushed to his limits.",["al"]={"smite weapons","what does smite pull out of the chest"},["q"]="What weapons does Mr. Smite use during the fight?"},{["a"]="Mr. Smite stands watch on the wooden piers of Ironclad Cove, the final cavern within the Deadmines, guarding the gangplank leading up to the giant Defias dreadnaught.",["al"]={"mr smite location","where is smite"},["q"]="Where can Mr. Smite be found?"},{["a"]="Smite keeps two stealthy Defias rogues hidden at his side, ready to ambush any trespassers who advance down the pier toward the ship.",["al"]={"smite adds","smite bodyguards"},["q"]="Does Mr. Smite fight alone?"},{["a"]="His signature tauren War Stomp sends shockwaves through the wooden dock, stunning entire parties of adventurers long enough for him to rearm himself from his footlocker and resume the assault with heavier weaponry.",["al"]={"smite stun","smite war stomp"},["q"]="What makes Mr. Smite so dangerous in close quarters?"}},["kw"]={"captain greenskin","deadmines","first mate","ironclad cove","mr smite","mr. smite","smite's mighty hammer","smite's reaver","tauren pirate","thief's blade"},["n"]="Mr. Smite",["s"]="Mr. Smite is the imposing tauren first mate serving aboard the Defias Brotherhood's flagship deep inside the Deadmines. An expert weaponmaster under Captain Greenskin, he commands the dockside approach to the hidden juggernaut with ruthless discipline. Intruders who face him must contend with his shifting arsenal and devastating physical strength.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Guarding the docks of Ironclad Cove, Mr. Smite serves as first mate to the goblin Captain Greenskin. While the Defias Brotherhood is predominantly composed of disenfranchised humans and allied goblin tinkerers, Smite stands as a striking anomaly: a massive, battle-hardened tauren far from the plains of Kalimdor. Tasked with maintaining strict order among a rowdy pirate crew, he ensures that the labor fitting out Edwin VanCleef's secret dreadnaught proceeds without disruption.",["t"]="First Mate of the Cove"},{["b"]="Smite is not merely a brute enforcer; he is a theatrical and versatile weaponmaster. He delights in toying with would-be heroes, deliberately prolonging combat to offer opponents a false sense of hope. When pressed, he unleashes a staggering, earth-shattering stomp that leaves foes stunned while he rummages through his nearby weapon chest. Beginning combat with a nimble dueling blade, he will escalate to twin cleaving reavers, and finally resort to his colossal two-handed warhammer when thoroughly provoked.",["t"]="A Deadly Weaponmaster"}}}}}
t["npc:mull-thunderhorn"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,359,29.438.0,37.540.1,24.237.0,54.293.0,44.271.0,54.266.0,33.268.0,27.268.0",["h"]="cc4114",["n"]="Mull Tronacuerno",["s"]="Mull Tronacuerno. Mull Tronacuerno es un anciano tauren que reside en el Poblado Pezuña de Sangre, en Mulgore. Profundamente devoto de la Madre Tierra y del equilibrio de la tierra, vela por los pozos de agua sagrados dispersos por las llanuras. Mientras explotadores forasteros amenazan las aguas vivificantes de la región, Mull guía a los jóvenes tauren a través de los rituales necesarios para purificar los manantiales ancestrales. Haciendo guardia en el Poblado Pezuña de Sangre, Mull Tronacuerno carga con el peso del bienestar espiritual de Mulgore. Las tribus nómadas se han reunido bajo el mando del Gran jefe Cairne Pezuña de Sangre para establecer un hogar permanente, pero sus tierras ya se encuentran asediadas por la codicia y la expansión imprudente. Mull sirve como ancla espiritual para los jóvenes valientes que salen del Campamento Narache, llamándolos a salvaguardar los recursos vitales de sus ancestros.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Druids share Mull's urgency, witnessing firsthand how the corrupted water wells poison the balance of Mulgore's wildlife.",["class:Shaman"]="Shaman will recognize Mull's reliance on elemental harmony, as his cleansing totems utilize ancestral spirits to mend waters torn by mechanical greed.",["faction:Horde"]="Mull's struggle underscores the Horde's friction with unaligned, exploitative organizations like the Venture Company that strip Kalimdor's riches without consent.",["race:Tauren"]="For the tauren, Mull Thunderhorn represents tribal memory and ancestral duty, guiding young braves in protecting the sacred plains against greedy foreign invaders."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Mull Thunderhorn is a tauren quest giver situated in Bloodhoof Village in Mulgore. He acts as a guardian of the sacred water wells in the area, offering rites and rituals to keep the earth and its waters pure from external contamination.",["al"]={"mull thunderhorn lore","who is mull","bloodhoof village mull"},["q"]="Who is Mull Thunderhorn?"},{["a"]="The ancestral water wells—such as the Winterhoof, Thunderhorn, and Wildmane wells—are life-giving sources for the tribes and wildlife of Mulgore. Intrusive operations nearby have tainted these sacred springs with noxious runoff and pollution, threatening the natural balance of the plains.",["al"]={"why are wells poisoned","water wells mulgore","winterhoof well poisoned"},["q"]="Why is Mull Thunderhorn worried about the water wells?"},{["a"]="The pollution is caused by the Venture Company, a reckless goblin enterprise establishing industrial mining and logging footholds across the edges of Mulgore. Their operations show no regard for the sacred landscape, spilling industrial toxins into the local water table.",["al"]={"who poisoned the water","venture co in mulgore","who tainted the wells"},["q"]="Who is polluting the water wells in Mulgore?"},{["a"]="The water wells hold deep ancestral and spiritual significance tied to the founding lineages of the tauren tribes—including the Thunderhorn, Winterhoof, and Wildmane clans. Cleansing them is viewed as a sacred rite of passage and cultural duty for maturing tauren.",["al"]={"tauren only quests","why only tauren","mull thunderhorn requirements"},["q"]="Why do Mull's purification quests only involve tauren?"},{["a"]="Mull instructs travelers to assemble specially consecrated totems imbued with local natural reagents, such as claws and hides. Once consecrated, these totems are brought directly to the fouled wells to channel spiritual purification and wash away the unnatural toxins.",["al"]={"how to cleanse wells","cleansing totems","cleaning the water"},["q"]="How are the water wells purified?"},{["a"]="The Rite of Vision is a foundational spiritual journey undertaken by young tauren to commune with their ancestors and animal spirits. Initiates are sent to Zarlman Two-Moons in Bloodhoof Village to undertake this visionary trial as one of the Rites of the Earthmother.",["al"]={"rite of vision quest","what is rite of vision"},["q"]="What is the Rite of Vision?"}},["kw"]={"bloodhoof village","mulgore","mull thunderhorn","poison water","thunderhorn totem","venture company","water wells","wildmane cleansing","winterhoof cleansing"},["n"]="Mull Thunderhorn",["s"]="Mull Thunderhorn is a tauren elder residing in Bloodhoof Village in Mulgore. Deeply devoted to the Earth Mother and the balance of the land, he watches over the sacred water wells scattered across the plains. As outside exploiters threaten the region's lifegiving waters, Mull guides young tauren through the rituals required to cleanse the ancestral springs.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Standing watch in Bloodhoof Village, Mull Thunderhorn carries the weight of Mulgore's spiritual well-being. The nomadic tribes have gathered under High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof to establish a permanent home, yet their lands are already under siege by greed and reckless expansion. Mull serves as a spiritual anchor for the young braves stepping out of Camp Narache, calling upon them to safeguard the vital resources of their ancestors.",["t"]="Guardian of the Sacred Waters"},{["b"]="The primary crisis facing Mull is the sudden sickness spreading through Mulgore's water sources: the Winterhoof, Thunderhorn, and Wildmane water wells. This foul affliction is traced to the goblins of the Venture Company, an unscrupulous commercial outfit carving operations into the surrounding hills and dumping poisons into the local water table. Mull directs young tauren to prepare specific purification totems and perform cleansing rites at each ancestral well before the corruption spreads irrevocably into the land and its wildlife.",["t"]="Tainted Wells and the Venture Company"}}}}}
t["npc:mutanus-the-devourer"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="20,358,22.505.0,20.460.1,29.236.0,42.199.0,49.236.0,29.205.0,34.184.1,38.158.0",["h"]="bb2627",["n"]="Mutanus el Devorador",["s"]="Mutanus el Devorador. Mutanus el Devorador es un monstruoso y pálido múrloc manifestado directamente a partir de la Pesadilla Esmeralda. Al acecho en los rincones más oscuros de la mente de Naralex, el druida durmiente, emerge para devorar a cualquiera que intente romper el dominio de la Pesadilla sobre las Cuevas de los Lamentos. Matar a esta aberración retorcida es el paso final para liberar a Naralex de su tormentoso letargo. Cuando el druida elfo de la noche Naralex canalizó los manantiales subterráneos bajo Los Baldíos, su objetivo era devolver la vida a los páramos áridos conectándolos con El Sueño Esmeralda. En su lugar, una antigua corrupción conocida como la Pesadilla Esmeralda invadió sus pensamientos. Atrapado en una visión agonizante, los miedos subconscientes de Naralex tomaron forma física. La corrupción se aprovechó de una extraña y primaria repulsión en la psique del druida (su arraigado terror a los múrlocs) y la amplificó hasta convertirla en un inmenso depredador albino.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,1,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Mutanus represents the terrifying hazards of delving too deeply into the Emerald Dream without safeguards, as a fellow druid's mind was completely overtaken by corruption.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde cannot allow Mutanus and the Nightmare to corrupt the heart of the Barrens, threatening the vital oasis waters needed to sustain Durotar and Mulgore.",["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, Mutanus is a tragedy brought to life, embodying how Naralex's noble ambitions to heal the Barrens warped into a monstrous nightmare."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Mutanus the Devourer is an enormous, pale murloc-like aberration born from the Emerald Nightmare. He is not a normal denizen of Azeroth, but a living nightmare summoned into reality from the corrupted mind of the sleeping druid Naralex.",["al"]={"who is mutanus","what kind of creature is mutanus","is mutanus a murloc"},["q"]="What is Mutanus the Devourer?"},{["a"]="The Nightmare twisted Naralex's subconscious thoughts and drew out his worst personal enemy: murlocs. The corruption weaponized that deep-seated fear, manifesting it as a colossal albino monstrosity.",["al"]={"why murloc","why is mutanus a murloc","naralex murloc fear"},["q"]="Why does Mutanus look like a giant murloc?"},{["a"]="The dark presence corrupting the Emerald Dream ordered Mutanus to prevent anyone from breaking Naralex's slumber. When Naralex's disciples begin the awakening ritual, Mutanus crosses over into the physical cavern to devour the rescuers.",["al"]={"when does mutanus spawn","why summon mutanus","naralex ritual boss"},["q"]="Why does Mutanus appear at the end of the ritual?"},{["a"]="Mutanus originates from the Emerald Nightmare, the corrupted realm that has ensnared Naralex. Crossing over from the dreamscape into Azeroth, he even brought along strange relics like the Deep Fathom Ring.",["al"]={"mutanus origin","is mutanus from the nightmare","emerald nightmare mutanus"},["q"]="Where does Mutanus come from?"},{["a"]="Yes. Once Mutanus is slain, the nightmare's immediate hold over Naralex's mind is shattered, allowing his disciples to successfully awaken the druid and break the cavern's dark trance.",["al"]={"is naralex saved","what happens after mutanus dies","waking naralex"},["q"]="Does killing Mutanus save Naralex?"},{["a"]="Mutanus is an aberration woven from dark nightmare energies, making him naturally resilient against necrotic and shadow spells that would harm mundane beasts.",["al"]={"mutanus shadow immunity","shadow spells mutanus","is mutanus shadow immune"},["q"]="Why is Mutanus immune to shadow magic?"}},["kw"]={"albino murloc","barrens","deep fathom ring","devourer","emerald nightmare","murloc","mutanus","naralex","wailing caverns"},["n"]="Mutanus the Devourer",["s"]="Mutanus the Devourer is a monstrous, pale murloc manifested directly from the Emerald Nightmare. Lurking in the darkest recesses of the sleeping druid Naralex's mind, it emerges to devour anyone attempting to break the Nightmare's hold over the Wailing Caverns. Slaying this twisted aberration is the final step in freeing Naralex from his tormented slumber.",["sec"]={{["b"]="When the night elf druid Naralex tapped into the underground springs beneath the Barrens, he aimed to restore life to the arid wastes by connecting them to the Emerald Dream. Instead, an ancient corruption known as the Emerald Nightmare invaded his thoughts. Trapped in an agonizing vision, Naralex's subconscious fears took physical form. The corruption seized upon a bizarre, primal revulsion in the druid's psyche—his deep-seated terror of murlocs—and amplified it into an immense, albino predator.",["t"]="A Dreamer's Worst Fear"},{["b"]="Mutanus was sent forth into the waking world by the dark force infesting Naralex's mind, tasked with ensuring the druid never awakens. When a Disciple of Naralex performs the ritual to revive their master, Mutanus breaches the boundary between dream and reality. Along with his unnatural form, he brings alien relics from the dreamscape, such as the mysterious Deep Fathom Ring. Until Mutanus falls, Naralex remains a prisoner of his own corrupted imagination.",["t"]="The Waking Nightmare"}}}}}
t["npc:naralex"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="7,277,17.662.0,20.602.0,16.560.1,15.231.0,49.256.0,36.285.0,42.245.0,24.224.1,43.216.0",["h"]="b1cbb2",["n"]="Naralex",["s"]="Naralex. Naralex es un elfo de la noche druida que intentó restaurar los marchitos Baldíos para convertirlos en un bosque exuberante usando los poderes del Sueño Esmeralda. En su lugar, una oscura pesadilla se apoderó de su letargo, deformando las Cuevas de los Lamentos bajo tierra y transformando a sus seguidores en engendros venenosos. Mucho antes del Gran Cataclismo, las llanuras abrasadas por el sol de Los Baldíos fueron antaño un bosque vibrante. Al considerar esta pérdida como una tragedia, Naralex viajó al sur desde Darnassus con una cohorte de devotos discípulos para revertir la sequía. En las profundidades bajo la sabana, descubrió una intrincada red subterránea de manantiales y géiseres impetuosos, a los que llamó las Cuevas de los Lamentos por el viento aullante y el vapor que gemían a través de la roca. Creía que, al entrar en un profundo trance y canalizar las energías puras del Sueño Esmeralda hacia estas aguas subterráneas, el caudal vivificante alcanzaría la superficie y haría florecer todo el páramo.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,1,0},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Naralex serves as a grim cautionary tale to druids: meddling blindly with primal natural states or tapping too deeply into the Dream without caution can unleash catastrophic perversions of the wild.",["faction:Horde"]="A night elf's failed mystical experiment has polluted the heart of the Barrens, forcing Horde forces from the Crossroads to deal with the rampaging beasts boiling up from the cavern.",["race:NightElf"]="While Naralex sought to heal Kalimdor, his unchecked ambition deep in Horde territory brought disgrace to the Cenarion Circle and spawned the treacherous Druids of the Fang.",["race:Tauren"]="The twisted waters beneath the Barrens pose an immediate threat to the oasis pools and wildlife that sustain the tribes of Mulgore and the savannah."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Naralex is a night elf druid of the Cenarion Circle. He led an expedition into the Wailing Caverns with the goal of tapping into the Emerald Dream to turn the arid Barrens back into the lush forest it had been before the Sundering.",["al"]={"naralex lore","who is the sleeping elf","wailing caverns sleeper"},["q"]="Who is Naralex?"},{["a"]="He entered a meditative trance to channel energies directly from the Emerald Dream into the underground aquifers beneath the Barrens. However, an overwhelming nightmare seized his mind, trapping him in a fevered slumber that he cannot wake from on his own.",["al"]={"why is naralex sleeping","what is naralex doing","naralex trance"},["q"]="Why is Naralex asleep inside the Wailing Caverns?"},{["a"]="They were originally Naralex's faithful disciples. When the Emerald Nightmare corrupted Naralex's dream connection, the leaking malice drove his followers insane. They abandoned the Cenarion Circle, embraced serpent totems, and now protect his slumber to keep the corruption spreading.",["al"]={"druids of the fang origin","who are druids of the fang","naralex disciples"},["q"]="What created the Druids of the Fang?"},{["a"]="Naralex's sleeping body became an open conduit for the Emerald Nightmare. The foul dream energies seeped directly into the subterranean river system, warping the caverns' plants, crocodiles, raptors, and serpents into aggressive deviate mutants.",["al"]={"why is wailing caverns corrupted","deviate beasts origin","wailing caverns fungus"},["q"]="What caused the Wailing Caverns to mutate?"},{["a"]="Yes, with outside help. His remaining loyal disciple, Muyoh, works with adventurers willing to enter the depths, slay the twisted Druids of the Fang, and perform a ritual to break the grip of the nightmare on Naralex's mind.",["al"]={"how to save naralex","waking naralex","naralex quest"},["q"]="Can Naralex be awakened?"},{["a"]="Naralex learned that the Barrens was once a flourishing forest before the Great Sundering shattered Kalimdor. He saw its current arid condition as an ecological wound and wished to restore its ancient verdant canopy.",["al"]={"why regrow the barrens","naralex barrens goal","why the barrens"},["q"]="Why did Naralex want to change the Barrens?"}},["kw"]={"cenarion circle","deviate","druids of the fang","emerald dream","emerald nightmare","muyoh","naralex","the barrens","wailing caverns"},["n"]="Naralex",["s"]="Naralex is a night elf druid who sought to restore the parched Barrens to a lush forest using the powers of the Emerald Dream. Instead, his slumber was overtaken by a dark nightmare, twisting the Wailing Caverns beneath the earth and turning his followers into venomous fiends.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Long before the Great Sundering, the sun-scorched plains of the Barrens were once a vibrant forest. Viewing this loss as a tragedy, Naralex journeyed south from Darnassus with a cohort of devoted disciples to reverse the drought. Deep beneath the savannah, he discovered an intricate subterranean network of underground springs and rushing geysers, naming them the Wailing Caverns after the howling wind and steam that moaned through the rock. He believed that by entering a deep trance and channeling the pristine energies of the Emerald Dream into these subterranean waters, the life-giving flow would reach the surface and cause the entire wasteland to bloom.",["t"]="A Vision of Green"},{["b"]="Naralex seated himself in deep meditation deep within the subterranean caverns, but his noble design collapsed the moment his consciousness touched the realm of the Dream. Rather than finding peaceful fonts of wild nature, his mind was ensnared by a malignant, encroaching corruption—an Emerald Nightmare. The festering corruption seized the sleeping druid's body, transforming him into an open conduit through which dark energies bled into the living world. The pristine springs turned foul, sprouting mutated fungal blooms and warping the native beasts of the caverns into ravenous deviate horrors.",["t"]="The Waking Nightmare"},{["b"]="The nightmare did not stop with the wildlife. Naralex's own disciples, driven completely mad by the psychic backlash bleeding out of their master's trance, broke away from the traditions of the Cenarion Circle. Casting aside their reverence for balance, they took on serpent forms and renamed themselves the Druids of the Fang. Believing their twisted growth must spread across Kalimdor, they now guard Naralex's slumbering body to ensure he never wakes, leaving only a few loyal disciples, such as Muyoh, searching for allies brave enough to break the trance.",["t"]="Fallen Disciples"}}}}}
t["npc:oggleflint"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="10,398,21.372.0,21.392.0,28.262.0,18.116.0,30.168.0,37.178.0,39.194.0,57.155.0",["h"]="6ed5be",["n"]="Ogglesílex",["s"]="Ogglesílex. Ogglesílex es el cabecilla de la tribu de troggs que habita en las profundidades volcánicas de la Sima Ígnea, directamente bajo Orgrimmar. Antaño amo de toda la caverna subterránea, él y sus congéneres se han visto empujados hacia los túneles superiores por la llegada de los sectarios de la Hoja Ardiente. Ahora atrincherado cerca de la entrada, comanda a su salvaje manada y supone una amenaza inmediata para la capital de la Horda que se alza sobre ellos. Antes de que los sectarios de las sombras se infiltraran en la sima situada bajo Orgrimmar, Ogglesílex y sus troggs dominaban sin oposición los ardientes túneles subterráneos. Brutales y territoriales, forjaron un dominio primitivo entre la roca fundida. Aunque los troggs carecen prácticamente de civilización avanzada, Ogglesílex mantuvo una autoridad absoluta sobre la manada a base de pura fuerza bruta.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warrior"]="Facing Oggleflint means confronting a heavy brute who relies entirely on raw muscle and primal rage rather than armor or discipline.",["faction:Horde"]="Living directly beneath Thrall's fortress, Oggleflint's troggs represent a wild, unpredictable security risk right in the heart of Durotar.",["race:Orc"]="For young orcs proving their mettle in the trial of arms, slaying the chieftain lurking right under the Drag is an early test of martial discipline."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Oggleflint is a powerful trogg chieftain who leads the pack inhabiting Ragefire Chasm beneath the city of Orgrimmar.",["al"]={"oggleflint","who is oggleflint","ragefire trogg boss"},["q"]="Who is Oggleflint?"},{["a"]="He is located in the upper caverns of Ragefire Chasm, not far from the entrance tunnel, where his surviving clan made camp after being pushed out of the deeper reaches.",["al"]={"where is oggleflint","oggleflint location","find oggleflint"},["q"]="Where can Oggleflint be found?"},{["a"]="Troggs naturally dwell deep underground in subterranean volcanic networks. Oggleflint's pack claimed the fiery caverns beneath Durotar long before the Searing Blade cult arrived.",["al"]={"why are troggs under orgrimmar","ragefire trogg lore"},["q"]="Why are the troggs in Ragefire Chasm?"},{["a"]="Troggs are fiercely territorial and violent beasts by nature. Pushed toward the surface by cultists, Oggleflint and his followers pose an imminent danger to the Horde tunnels and the city above.",["al"]={"why kill oggleflint","why fight oggleflint"},["q"]="Why is Oggleflint hostile to the Horde?"},{["a"]="They are bitter enemies. The Searing Blade cultists invaded Ragefire Chasm and overpowered Oggleflint's troggs, driving the survivors into the upper caves.",["al"]={"searing blade and oggleflint","are troggs with the cult"},["q"]="What is Oggleflint's relationship with the Searing Blade?"}},["kw"]={"oggleflint","orgrimmar","ragefire chasm","searing blade","trogg"},["n"]="Oggleflint",["s"]="Oggleflint is the chieftain of the trogg tribe dwelling within the volcanic depths of Ragefire Chasm directly beneath Orgrimmar. Once master of the entire subterranean cavern, he and his kin have been pushed toward the upper tunnels by the arrival of the Searing Blade cultists. Now entrenched near the entrance, he commands his savage pack and poses an immediate threat to the Horde capital above.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before shadow cultists infiltrated the chasm beneath Orgrimmar, Oggleflint and his troggs ruled the fiery subterranean tunnels uncontested. Brutal and territorial, they carved out a primitive domain among the molten rock. Though troggs possess little in the way of advanced civilization, Oggleflint maintained absolute authority over the pack through sheer brute strength.",["t"]="Chieftain of the Deep"},{["b"]="The balance of power beneath the city shattered when the Searing Blade moved into the deepest chambers of Ragefire Chasm. Unable to match the dark magic and coordinated zealots of the cult, Oggleflint was forced to cede the lower tunnels. Retreating upward, the trogg chieftain now waits near the cavern entrance, striking at any outsiders while nursing grudges against the interlopers below.",["t"]="Displaced by the Cult"},{["b"]="Having displaced troggs directly beneath Thrall's capital is a hazard the Horde cannot tolerate. Pushed closer to the surface, Oggleflint's tribe is far too volatile to leave unchecked, threatening to spill into the Drag and Cleft of Shadows if left undisturbed.",["t"]="The Threat Beneath Orgrimmar"}}}}}
t["npc:old-serra-kis"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,285,25.465.0,15.368.0,39.130.0,42.257.0,31.183.0,34.166.0,43.147.0,49.181.0",["h"]="e7dd5a",["n"]="Viejo Serra'kis",["s"]="Viejo Serra'kis. El Viejo Serra'kis es un antiguo y descomunal trilladón que mora en las aguas subterráneas sumergidas de Cavernas de Brazanegra. Aunque los invasores del Martillo Crepuscular sacrificaron gran parte de la vida acuática del templo para aprovisionarse, esta enorme bestia resultó ser letal para cualquiera que intentara cazarla. Cuando los sectarios del Martillo Crepuscular descendieron a las sumergidas Ruinas del Santuario Lunar, masacraron la fauna nativa bajo las aguas para alimentarse. Sin embargo, bajo el Santuario Lunar, una criatura primigenia se negó a convertirse en presa. El Viejo Serra'kis, el trilladón más grande del templo sumergido, despachó rápidamente a cualquier sectario lo bastante insensato como para intentar clavarle un arpón. Con el tiempo, los cazadores abandonaron su empeño y dejaron al antiguo carnívoro tranquilo en su dominio acuático.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Druids of the wild will find Aquatic Form indispensable when diving into the lightless pool to confront this prehistoric predator.",["class:Shaman"]="Water Breathing spells granted by spiritual communion with the elements ensure your companions don't drown while grappling with the ancient thresher.",["class:Warlock"]="A warlock's ability to bestow Unending Breath turns an otherwise deadly, airless subterranean ambush into a manageable fight."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Old Serra'kis is a massive, ancient threshadon—a long-necked, aquatic reptile native to the lakes and coastal waters of Azeroth.",["al"]={"what is serrakis","is serrakis a hydra","serrakis creature type"},["q"]="What kind of creature is Old Serra'kis?"},{["a"]="The cult slaughtered most aquatic life beneath the Moonshrine Ruins for food, but Serra'kis was too powerful and cunning. Cultists who persisted in attempting to hunt him inevitably ended up as his meals instead, leading the cult to avoid his cave entirely.",["al"]={"why is serrakis still alive","twilights hammer serrakis"},["q"]="Why didn't the Twilight's Hammer kill him?"},{["a"]="He lurks in a submerged cavern beneath the water surrounding the Moonshrine Sanctum within Blackfathom Deeps. Swimmers must dive under the ruins into an airless pool to encounter him.",["al"]={"how to find serrakis","serrakis location","where is old serrakis"},["q"]="Where is Old Serra'kis located?"},{["a"]="Beyond fighting entirely underwater without natural pockets of air, Old Serra'kis leeches shadow energy from all nearby foes to heal his own wounds throughout combat.",["al"]={"serrakis abilities","how to beat serrakis"},["q"]="What makes fighting him dangerous?"},{["a"]="No. Unlike other beasts corrupted or trained by the cult, Old Serra'kis remains a completely untamed wild predator defending his subterranean lair.",["al"]={"is serrakis a cultist pet","who controls serrakis"},["q"]="Does Serra'kis serve the Twilight's Hammer?"},{["a"]="His enclosed cave offers no ceiling air pockets, forcing underwater fighters to either manage their breath, use magical water-breathing aid, or kite the beast out toward open water.",["al"]={"drowning serrakis","breath underwater serrakis"},["q"]="Can you breathe during the battle with Serra'kis?"}},["kw"]={"blackfathom deeps","forgotten pool","moonshrine sanctum","old serrakis","serrakis","threshadon","twilight's hammer","underwater boss"},["n"]="Old Serra'kis",["s"]="Old Serra'kis is an ancient, massive threshadon dwelling in the submerged subterranean waters of Blackfathom Deeps. While the invading Twilight's Hammer culled much of the temple's aquatic life for provisions, this enormous beast proved entirely lethal to any who attempted to hunt it.",["sec"]={{["b"]="When the Twilight's Hammer cultists descended upon the sunken Moonshrine Ruins, they slaughtered the native wildlife beneath the waters for sustenance. Yet beneath the Moonshrine Sanctum, one primeval creature refused to become prey. Old Serra'kis, the largest threshadon in the sunken temple, made short work of any cultist brazen enough to spear him. Eventually, the hunters abandoned their efforts, leaving the ancient carnivore undisturbed in his watery domain.",["t"]="Unconquered in the Depths"},{["b"]="Reaching Old Serra'kis requires plunging deep beneath the temple floor into a flooded cavern beneath the ruins. Lacking air pockets, the cave itself is as deadly as the beast within. Those who corner him find that Serra'kis possesses an unnatural shadow-leeching resilience, draining the life from his attackers while sustaining his own vitality in the murky darkness.",["t"]="A Hidden Threat"}}}}}
t["npc:orgnil-soulscar"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,308,21.388.0,37.458.1,23.216.0,41.210.0,41.233.0,35.101.0,37.240.0,37.175.0",["h"]="3a6731",["n"]="Orgnil Escaralma",["s"]="Orgnil Escaralma. Orgnil Escaralma es un investigador orco apostado en Cerrotajo, en el centro de Durotar. Ejerce como agente de la paz informal, coordinando la defensa y la información contra amenazas internas para la incipiente nación. Su principal preocupación es la sombra que proyecta la secta del Filo Ardiente en los cañones de Durotar. Apostado en Cerrotajo, Orgnil Escaralma asume la sombría responsabilidad de rastrear la subversión y las amenazas insidiosas por todo Durotar. Mientras las patrullas de brutos miran hacia el exterior, hacia los enclaves de la Alianza y las partidas de asalto centauros, Orgnil se centra en la podredumbre que se gesta desde dentro. Recopila informes de exploradores de toda la región, uniendo pruebas de corrupción ritual y reuniones ilícitas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warlock"]="Warlocks must tread carefully around Orgnil, as his entire focus is hunting down and eradicating unchecked demonic corruption within Durotar's borders.",["faction:Horde"]="Orgnil ensures that while the Horde looks outward to build a new nation, its heartland is not hollowed out by cultists from within.",["race:Orc"]="For young orcs, Orgnil represents the frontline against the demonic taint that once enslaved the clans, reminding new recruits of the vigilance required to keep their new homeland pure."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Orgnil Soulscar is an orc official based in Razor Hill who acts as an investigator and coordinator for Durotar's defense. He directs warriors and scouts against covert dangers threatening the newly settled orc lands.",["al"]={"who is orgnil","orgnil soulscar lore","razor hill quest giver"},["q"]="Who is Orgnil Soulscar?"},{["a"]="Orgnil is dedicated to rooting out the Burning Blade cult. He sees their presence in Durotar's hidden caverns and their corruptive fel magic as a lethal threat to the fresh start Thrall envisions for the Horde.",["al"]={"what does orgnil want","orgnil enemies","who does orgnil fight"},["q"]="What threat is Orgnil most worried about?"},{["a"]="Margoz is a knowledgeable hermit living north of Razor Hill who understands the dark signs and rituals of the Burning Blade. Orgnil directs scouts to Margoz to decipher the cult's movements and unravel the brewing magical corruption.",["al"]={"why margoz","orgnil and margoz","who is margoz to orgnil"},["q"]="Why does Orgnil send travelers to Margoz?"},{["a"]="Orgnil is stationed outdoors in the settlement of Razor Hill, near the central crossroads of Durotar.",["al"]={"orgnil location","where is orgnil","find orgnil soulscar"},["q"]="Where can Orgnil Soulscar be found?"},{["a"]="The Burning Blade is a sinister cult beholden to demonic masters and the Shadow Council. They hide in ravines like Skull Rock and the Dustwind Cave, attempting to poison Durotar's wildlife and seduce young orcs back to demonic subservience.",["al"]={"burning blade durotar","burning blade cult","who are burning blade"},["q"]="What is the Burning Blade in Durotar?"},{["a"]="Orgnil operates as part of the regional defense apparatus centered in Razor Hill, carrying out the Warchief's mandate to safeguard Durotar from sedition and demonic influence.",["al"]={"orgnil thrall","is orgnil warchief guard"},["q"]="Does Orgnil work directly for Thrall?"}},["kw"]={"burning blade","durotar","margoz","orgnil soulscar","razor hill","shadow council","skull rock"},["n"]="Orgnil Soulscar",["s"]="Orgnil Soulscar is an orc investigator stationed at Razor Hill in central Durotar. He serves as an informal officer of the peace, coordinating defense and intelligence against internal threats to the fledgling nation. His primary concern is the shadow cast by the Burning Blade cult within Durotar's canyons.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Positioned at Razor Hill, Orgnil Soulscar takes on the grim responsibility of tracking subversion and insidious threats across Durotar. While grunt patrols look outward toward Alliance footholds and centaur raiding parties, Orgnil focuses on rot brewing from within. He collects reports from scouts across the region, piecing together evidence of ritual corruption and illicit gatherings.",["t"]="Watcher of Razor Hill"},{["b"]="Orgnil's chief focus is the clandestine resurgence of the Burning Blade cult, whose warlocks hide in caves such as Skull Rock. Knowing the devastation fel magic brought upon the orcish people in past generations, Orgnil refuses to let demon worship gain another foothold near Orgrimmar. He directs trusted recruits to strike down cultists, gather ritual talismans, and consult with local hermits and shamans like Margoz to understand the dark magics at play.",["t"]="Hunting the Shadow Council's Remnants"}}}}}
t["npc:orgrim-doomhammer"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,342,20.674.0,15.625.0,26.251.0,30.231.0,41.218.0,33.251.0",["h"]="cc56bc",["n"]="Orgrim Martillo Maldito",["s"]="Orgrim Martillo Maldito. Orgrim Martillo Maldito fue el Jefe de Guerra supremo de la Antigua Horda durante la Segunda Guerra, recordado como uno de los mayores guerreros orcos de la historia. Aunque murió liberando los campos de internamiento en las Tierras Altas de Arathi, su legado perdura en la capital de Orgrimmar y a través de Thrall, quien heredó su poderoso martillo de guerra y su armadura de placas negra. Originalmente el segundo al mando de Puño Negro en el Clan Roca Negra, Orgrim rechazó la sangre demoníaca ofrecida por Gul'dan, aunque ocultó sus dudas bajo una feroz lealtad. Hacia el final de la Primera Guerra, asqueado por la traición del Consejo de la Sombra y el asesinato de su amigo de la infancia Durotan, Orgrim mató a Puño Negro en combate honorable. Tras asumir el manto de Jefe de Guerra, purgó implacablemente a los brujos de Gul'dan y lideró a la Horda a través de los Reinos del Este durante la Segunda Guerra. Aunque fue un estratega devastador que llevó a los reinos humanos al borde de la ruina, finalmente fue derrotado y capturado frente a la Cumbre de Roca Negra después de que la traición de Gul'dan dividiera sus fuerzas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="To the Alliance, Doomhammer remains a grim symbol of the near-destruction of the Eastern Kingdoms during the Second War, having butchered countless champions before his defeat at Blackrock Spire.",["race:Orc"]="Orcs revere Orgrim Doomhammer as the liberator who freed their people from lethargy and interned enslavement, choosing honor over demonic subjugation."},["faq"]={{["a"]="He was the Chieftain of the Blackrock clan and the Warchief who commanded the Horde during the Second War. After escaping human captivity years later, he fought alongside Thrall to liberate their imprisoned kin until his death in the Arathi Highlands.",["al"]={"who is doomhammer","orgrim doomhammer background","who was warchief doomhammer"},["q"]="Who was Orgrim Doomhammer?"},{["a"]="Orgrim was slain during an assault on a human internment camp in the Arathi Highlands, struck from behind by a knight's lance. Thrall took up his mantle, and the site of that victory was named Hammerfall in memory of his sacrifice.",["al"]={"orgrim doomhammer death","how did doomhammer die","who killed doomhammer"},["q"]="How did Orgrim Doomhammer die?"},{["a"]="Thrall named the fortified city in Durotar to honor his mentor and predecessor. Orgrim saw the promise in Thrall and named him the new Warchief, ensuring the Horde would rebuild on honor rather than demonic corruption.",["al"]={"why is it called orgrimmar","orgrimmar namesake","city named after orgrim"},["q"]="Why is the Horde capital named Orgrimmar?"},{["a"]="No. Orgrim feigned humility, telling Blackhand and Gul'dan that a mere servant was not worthy to drink from the same cup as the Warchief. This clever excuse allowed him to retain his clarity and eventually destroy Gul'dan's Shadow Council from within.",["al"]={"did doomhammer drink blood","was orgrim corrupted","orgrim demon blood"},["q"]="Did Orgrim drink the demon blood?"}},["kw"]={"blackhand","blackrock","doomhammer","hammerfall","orgrim","orgrimmar","thrall","warchief"},["n"]="Orgrim Doomhammer",["s"]="Orgrim Doomhammer was the supreme Warchief of the Old Horde throughout the Second War, remembered as one of the greatest orc warriors in history. Though he died liberating the internment camps in the Arathi Highlands, his legacy endures in the capital of Orgrimmar and through Thrall, who inherited his mighty warhammer and black plate armor.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Originally second-in-command to Blackhand of the Blackrock clan, Orgrim refused the demonic blood offered by Gul'dan, though he concealed his doubts beneath fierce loyalty. Near the close of the First War, disgusted by the Shadow Council's treachery and the murder of his childhood friend Durotan, Orgrim slew Blackhand in honorable combat. Assuming the mantle of Warchief, he ruthlessly purged Gul'dan's warlocks and led the Horde across the Eastern Kingdoms during the Second War. Though a devastating strategist who pushed human kingdoms to the brink of ruin, he was ultimately defeated and captured outside Blackrock Spire after the betrayal of Gul'dan split his forces.",["t"]="Rise of the Warchief"},{["b"]="Escaping human captivity, Doomhammer lived in hiding until he met Thrall, Durotan's orphaned son. Reinvigorated by the young shaman's vision, Orgrim rallied what was left of the orcish clans to storm the internment camps and break their people free. During a fierce battle at an encampment in the Arathi Highlands, the Warchief was struck down from behind by a lance. As he lay dying, he bestowed his black plate armor, his ancestral weapon—the Doomhammer—and the title of Warchief upon Thrall. In his honor, the liberated outpost was renamed Hammerfall, and the newly founded capital in Durotar was christened Orgrimmar.",["t"]="Fall and Legacy"}}}}}
t["npc:overlord-ramtusk"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,302,22.450.0,29.397.0,24.190.0,36.120.0,44.164.0,34.121.0,39.181.0,23.192.0",["h"]="50274e",["n"]="Señor Supremo Colmicarnero",["s"]="Señor Supremo Colmicarnero. El Señor Supremo Colmicarnero es el curtido comandante de las fuerzas militares de la tribu Caramuerte en las profundidades de Horado Rajacieno. Siendo un imponente y veterano guerrero jabaespín, su pellejo está profundamente marcado por décadas de brutales enfrentamientos a lo largo de Los Baldíos. Derrotarlo supone quebrar la columna vertebral marcial de los defensores de Horado. El Señor Supremo Colmicarnero ha sobrevivido a décadas en una de las fronteras más violentas de Kalimdor. Su pellejo grueso y curtido está repleto de profundas cicatrices obtenidas en escaramuzas contra partidas de asalto centauras, arpías salvajes, orcos invasores y aguerridos bravos tauren. Aunque la avanzada edad ralentiza a muchos guerreros, los curtidos instintos y la resistencia física de Colmicarnero no han hecho más que endurecerse, lo que le permite gobernar la guarnición permanente de Horado Rajacieno con una autoridad implacable.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warrior"]="Ramtusk represents pure, brutal martial veteranhood, relying on thunderous strikes and commanding battle shouts rather than shamans' geomancy or thorn magic.",["race:Orc"]="The quilboar have actively raided Horde settlements since the founding of Durotar and the Barrens outposts. Breaking Ramtusk's military command secures the Southern Barrens.",["race:Tauren"]="For generations, the nomadic tribes of the Barrens fought bitter skirmishes against Ramtusk and his marauders; putting him down avenges fallen braves."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Overlord Ramtusk is the supreme military commander of the Death's Head quilboar in Razorfen Kraul. He is an imposing, heavily scarred veteran who has fought every major power in the Barrens.",["al"]={"who is ramtusk","ramtusk lore","overlord ramtusk"},["q"]="Who is Overlord Ramtusk?"},{["a"]="He commands his elite guards from within the thorny heart of Razorfen Kraul, located at the southern tip of the Barrens.",["al"]={"ramtusk location","where is ramtusk","overlord ramtusk map"},["q"]="Where can Overlord Ramtusk be found?"},{["a"]="His scarred hide tells the tale of countless clashes across the Barrens against centaur packs, territorial harpies, newly arrived orcs, and native tauren defenders.",["al"]={"ramtusk enemies","who gave ramtusk scars","ramtusk battle history"},["q"]="What enemies has Ramtusk fought in the past?"},{["a"]="He is the high military leader of the Death's Head tribe, the dominant quilboar faction entrenched within Razorfen Kraul.",["al"]={"ramtusk faction","ramtusk tribe","what quilboar tribe is ramtusk"},["q"]="What tribe does Ramtusk belong to?"},{["a"]="As the supreme commander of the Death's Head forces, Ramtusk's death deals a crippling blow to the quilboar military hierarchy, throwing their defensive line into complete disarray.",["al"]={"why kill ramtusk","take them down quest","ramtusk bounty"},["q"]="Why is Ramtusk targeted by adventurers?"},{["a"]="Ramtusk fights as a classic battle-hardened warrior, using demoralizing cries to empower his cohort, crushing shockwaves to stagger enemies, and coordinating alongside elite ranged bodyguards.",["al"]={"ramtusk tactics","ramtusk combat style","ramtusk abilities"},["q"]="How does Ramtusk fight?"}},["kw"]={"barrens","deaths head","overlord ramtusk","quilboar","ramtusk","razorfen kraul"},["n"]="Overlord Ramtusk",["s"]="Overlord Ramtusk is the grizzled commander of the Death's Head tribe's military forces deep within Razorfen Kraul. A massive, aging quilboar warrior, his hide is heavily scarred from decades of brutal clashes across the Barrens. Striking him down shatters the martial backbone of the Kraul's defenders.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Overlord Ramtusk has survived decades in one of Kalimdor's most violent frontiers. His thick, leathery hide is crisscrossed with deep scars earned in skirmishes against centaur raiding parties, feral harpies, encroaching orcs, and stalwart tauren braves. While advanced age slows many warriors, Ramtusk's seasoned instincts and physical resilience have only hardened, allowing him to rule Razorfen Kraul's standing garrison with unyielding authority.",["t"]="Veteran of the Barrens"},{["b"]="Within the winding brambles of the Kraul, Ramtusk directs the military forces of the Death's Head quilboar. As their warlord, he maintains tight discipline among the bristled fighters defending the tribe's sanctum. Flanked by elite marksmen, Ramtusk fights like a frontline berserker, bellowing rallying shouts and unleashing earth-shattering slams that can break opposing battle lines in seconds.",["t"]="Commander of the Death's Head"}}}}}
t["npc:ozzie-togglevolt"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,295,20.460.0,21.367.0,24.216.0,29.170.0,23.212.0,38.179.0,43.256.0,29.196.0",["h"]="322c1b",["n"]="Oci Voltiflop",["s"]="Oci Voltiflop. Oci Voltiflop es un ingeniero gnomo y superviviente de la caída de Gnomeregan que actualmente opera desde la nevada aldea de Kharanos, en Dun Morogh. Atormentado por la tragedia que asoló a su pueblo, trabaja junto a su compañero Razzle Energiodentado para investigar un remedio para los gnomos parias irradiados. Oci Voltiflop se encontraba en el interior de las maravillas subterráneas de Gnomeregan cuando sobrevino la catástrofe. Cuando se liberó la lluvia radiactiva tóxica por los conductos para frenar la invasión de los troggs, Oci estaba junto a su compañero gnomo, Gnoarn. Una repentina descarga radiactiva alcanzó a Gnoarn de lleno, alterándolo para siempre ante los ojos de Oci. Aunque Oci logró salir con vida a la superficie y alcanzar el refugio de Dun Morogh, el espantoso recuerdo de aquel desastre jamás lo abandonó.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Stationed right outside Ironforge in Kharanos, Ozzie aids travelers while maintaining Alliance footholds in the frigid hills of Dun Morogh.",["profession:Engineering"]="Ozzie showcases the trial-and-error realities of gnome craftsmanship, where devices can backfire dramatically in combat or yield ingenious breakthroughs in biochemical decontamination.",["race:Gnome"]="For gnome adventurers, Ozzie represents the grief and determination of the survivors of Gnomeregan, refusing to abandon irradiated kin to their fate."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Ozzie Togglevolt is a gnomish engineer residing in Kharanos in Dun Morogh. He fled the radioactive devastation of Gnomeregan and now dedicates his technical expertise toward finding a cure for his afflicted brethren.",["al"]={"who is ozzie","ozzie togglevolt lore","kharanos gnome ozzie"},["q"]="Who is Ozzie Togglevolt?"},{["a"]="Ozzie and his colleague Razzle Sprysprocket are researching a method to cleanse the toxic irradiation that turned so many of their kin into madness-stricken leper gnomes.",["al"]={"what is ozzie researching","ozzie leper gnome cure","cure for leper gnomes"},["q"]="What is Ozzie trying to cure?"},{["a"]="Gnoarn was with Ozzie in Gnomeregan when the toxic vents were unleashed. Ozzie witnessed a radioactive bolt strike Gnoarn directly, a tragic incident that drove Ozzie's obsession with reversing the contamination.",["al"]={"ozzie and gnoarn","what happened to gnoarn","who is gnoarn"},["q"]="Who is Gnoarn to Ozzie?"},{["a"]="Ozzie works alongside Razzle Sprysprocket. Together, they tinker in Kharanos, developing concoctions and gathering contaminated field specimens to analyze the radioactive fallout.",["al"]={"ozzie partner","who is razzle","razzle sprysprocket"},["q"]="Who is working with Ozzie in Kharanos?"},{["a"]="Yes. When a massive Frostmane troll assaulted Kharanos, Ozzie and Razzle attempted to fend it off by hurling what they thought were impact grenades, only to discover they were actually delayed time bombs before fellow inventor Lazlo Grindwidget intervened.",["al"]={"ozzie troll attack","frostmane troll kharanos","ozzie grenades"},["q"]="Did Ozzie help defend Kharanos from trolls?"},{["a"]="Ozzie enlists travelers in Dun Morogh to gather irradiated residues and components from around Gnomeregan through tasks such as 'The Day After', 'Gnogaine', and 'The Only Cure is More Green Glow'.",["al"]={"ozzie quests","togglevolt quests","what quests does ozzie give"},["q"]="What quests does Ozzie offer?"}},["kw"]={"dun morogh","gnoarn","gnomeregan","kharanos","leper gnome","ozzie","radiation","razzle","sprysprocket","togglevolt"},["n"]="Ozzie Togglevolt",["s"]="Ozzie Togglevolt is a gnome engineer and survivor of Gnomeregan's fall, currently operating out of the snowy village of Kharanos in Dun Morogh. Haunted by the tragedy that struck his people, he works alongside his partner Razzle Sprysprocket to research a remedy for the irradiated leper gnomes.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Ozzie Togglevolt was inside the subterranean wonders of Gnomeregan when catastrophe struck. When the toxic fallout was vented throughout the corridors to stem the trogg invasion, Ozzie stood right beside his fellow gnome, Gnoarn. A sudden radioactive discharge struck Gnoarn directly, altering him forever before Ozzie's eyes. Though Ozzie made it to the surface alive and reached the haven of Dun Morogh, the horrifying memory of that disaster never left him.",["t"]="Escape from the Deep"},{["b"]="Now established in Kharanos, Ozzie spends his days tinkering alongside Razzle Sprysprocket. Despite minor mishaps and defensive scrambles against encroaching Frostmane trolls, their primary technological and scientific endeavor remains intensely personal: finding a way to reverse the horrific mutagenic fallout of their lost home and cure the suffering leper gnomes.",["t"]="The Kharanos Workshop"}}}}}
t["npc:pelturas-whitemoon"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,409,30.472.0,34.481.1,15.414.1,26.217.0,40.252.0,38.173.0,40.257.0,47.274.0,61.174.0",["h"]="08e076",["n"]="Pelturas Lunablanca",["s"]="Pelturas Lunablanca. Pelturas Lunablanca es un padre elfo de la noche que vive en Astranaar y cuya joven hija, Relara, ha sido víctima de una terrible enfermedad corruptora. Desesperado por salvarla, colabora estrechamente con el herborista local Orendil Hojasangre y con campeones viajeros de la Alianza para reunir remedios sagrados de las tierras salvajes circundantes. Su misión para sanar a Relara lleva a los aventureros a algunas de las ruinas y arboledas sagradas más antiguas de Vallefresno. Afincado bajo las serenas ramas de Astranaar, Pelturas Lunablanca lleva la vida tranquila típica de los kaldorei del bosque, aventurándose a menudo con su joven hija Relara a recoger relucientes piedras lunares alrededor del Lago Cielo Estrellado. Sin embargo, cuando Relara cae gravemente enferma por una misteriosa aflicción, su apacible mundo se desmorona en una frenética desesperación. Astranaar está sitiada en muchos frentes, pero para Pelturas no hay nada en el gran bosque más importante que salvar a su hija.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Priest"]="The cleansing rites and holy reagents consecrated to Elune showcase the healing power and sacred reverence that the Sisterhood of Elune brings to night elf culture.",["faction:Alliance"]="Helping Pelturas save his daughter reinforces the Alliance's commitment to defending and aiding the Kaldorei settlements in Kalimdor.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The sequence of natural draughts, poultices, and botanical tinctures needed for Relara highlights the deep connection between Kaldorei medicine and herbal lore.",["race:NightElf"]="Pelturas's struggle reflects the vulnerability of everyday Kaldorei families as ancient glades fall prey to corruption and regional conflict."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Pelturas Whitemoon is a night elf resident of Astranaar in central Ashenvale. He is best known for seeking the aid of passing Alliance travelers to gather sacred ingredients to cure his seriously ill daughter, Relara.",["al"]={"pelturas","who is pelturas whitemoon","pelturas astranaar"},["q"]="Who is Pelturas Whitemoon?"},{["a"]="Relara suffers from a sudden, virulent disease that causes a severe fever and deep weakness. The sickness appears tied to the unnatural corruption spreading through Ashenvale's wilds, resisting mundane medicine and requiring sacred reagents to cleanse.",["al"]={"relara illness","why is relara sick","relara disease"},["q"]="What is wrong with his daughter, Relara?"},{["a"]="Pelturas seeks council from Orendil Broadleaf, a knowledgeable local night elf who prescribes traditional Kaldorei remedies, including cleansing stones and herbal poultices.",["al"]={"pelturas herbalist","who helps relara","orendil broadleaf pelturas"},["q"]="Who helps Pelturas treat the sickness?"},{["a"]="Saving Relara requires a progression of treatments: an initial herbal draught from Orendil, a purifying Elune's Tear, powdered stardust from ancient ruins to break her burning fever, and a moonstone from Fallen Sky Lake brewed into tea to restore her vigor.",["al"]={"cure reagents pelturas","relara cure ingredients","what cures relara"},["q"]="What reagents are needed to cure Relara?"},{["a"]="Fallen Sky Lake was a place where Pelturas and Relara used to spend time together gathering moonstones. The lake has recently been overtaken by hostile Shadethicket bog beasts, forcing Pelturas to ask adventurers to retrieve the moonstone needed for his daughter's recovery.",["al"]={"fallen sky lake pelturas","moonstone fallen sky lake"},["q"]="Why is Fallen Sky Lake significant to Pelturas?"},{["a"]="No. Pelturas is a civilian town resident of Astranaar, representing the everyday Kaldorei families who live within Ashenvale and suffer from the forest's encroaching dangers.",["al"]={"is pelturas a sentinel","pelturas faction role"},["q"]="Is Pelturas a member of the Cenarion Circle or the Sentinels?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","astranaar","elune's tear","fallen sky lake","moonstone","orendil broadleaf","pelturas","relara","ruins of stardust","whitemoon"},["n"]="Pelturas Whitemoon",["s"]="Pelturas Whitemoon is a night elf father dwelling in Astranaar whose young daughter, Relara, has been struck by a terrible, corrupting illness. Desperate to save her, he works closely with local herbalist Orendil Broadleaf and traveling Alliance champions to gather sacred remedies from the surrounding wilds. His quest to heal Relara takes adventurers into some of Ashenvale's oldest sacred groves and ruins.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Residing in the serene boughs of Astranaar, Pelturas Whitemoon lives the quiet life typical of forest-dwelling Kaldorei, often venturing out with his young daughter Relara to collect shimmering moonstones around Fallen Sky Lake. However, when Relara falls critically ill with a mysterious affliction, his quiet world collapses into frantic desperation. Astranaar is besieged on many fronts, but for Pelturas, nothing in the great forest matters more than saving his child.",["t"]="A Father's Plight in Astranaar"},{["b"]="Normal herbal remedies fail to break Relara's condition, prompting Pelturas to turn to the herbalist Orendil Broadleaf. Treating the affliction requires rare and sacred reagents tied to the land and the Moon Goddess, including an Elune's Tear and shimmering stardust from ancient Kaldorei ruins to cool her burning fever. Each step only narrowly keeps death at bay, highlighting how deeply the corruption spreading through Ashenvale's soil and waters has begun to touch its people.",["t"]="Ancient Cures and Corrupted Groves"},{["b"]="To fully restore Relara's vitality, Pelturas seeks a moonstone from the Shadethicket Oracle at Fallen Sky Lake. The lake, once a tranquil spot where father and daughter peacefully gathered stones together, has grown perilous due to the violent emergence of corrupted bog beasts. By crushing the recovered moonstone into a restorative tea, Pelturas finally breaks the lingering weakness, restoring Relara to health.",["t"]="Fallen Sky Lake"}}}}}
t["npc:priestess-alathea"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,336,34.465.0,27.429.0,25.201.0,30.198.0,35.165.0,48.240.0,44.226.0,57.212.0",["h"]="9437a1",["n"]="Sacerdotisa Alathea",["s"]="Sacerdotisa Alathea. La Sacerdotisa Alathea es una instructora de sacerdotes elfa de la noche que reside en las apacibles estancias del Templo de la Luna, en Darnassus. Consagrada a la Diosa de la Luna, guía a los novicios en las artes sagradas y en las bendiciones raciales otorgadas por Elune. Sus enseñanzas ayudan a los practicantes elfos de la noche a armonizar sus mentes con plegarias defensivas y magia celestial. Erguida bajo las imponentes alturas plateadas del mayor santuario de Darnassus, la Sacerdotisa Alathea sirve a las Hermanas de Elune como instructora y guía espiritual. A medida que los iniciados elfos de la noche avanzan más allá de las tranquilas ramas de Cañada Umbría, se les encomienda acudir al Templo de la Luna para profundizar en su pacto con la Diosa. Alathea se encuentra entre las sacerdotisas dispuestas a transmitir conocimientos sagrados a quienes consagran su vida a la sanación, la protección y la luz divina.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Priest"]="Priestess Alathea is a vital contact for Alliance priests visiting Darnassus, offering rank advancements and guiding kaldorei acolytes to their unique celestial powers.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alathea opens the Temple of the Moon's teachings to all traveling members of the Alliance who study the clerical arts.",["race:NightElf"]="As a priestess in the heart of Darnassus, Alathea represents the living spiritual traditions of the Sisterhood of Elune that have protected the kaldorei for millennia."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Priestess Alathea is a kaldorei priest trainer stationed inside the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus, responsible for training budding priests and guiding night elf acolytes through their sacred trials.",["al"]={"who is alathea","alathea darnassus","alathea priest trainer"},["q"]="Who is Priestess Alathea?"},{["a"]="She offers standard priest spell training as well as specific trials for night elf racials, including Starshards and Elune's Grace, which channel the direct power and protection of the Moon Goddess.",["al"]={"alathea abilities","alathea spells","priest spells darnassus"},["q"]="What abilities does she teach?"},{["a"]="She resides on the ground floor of the Temple of the Moon in the southern reaches of Darnassus, surrounded by the sanctuary's luminous waters and fellow priestesses.",["al"]={"where is alathea","alathea location"},["q"]="Where can I find Priestess Alathea?"},{["a"]="As kaldorei priests advance in their training, novice instructors across Teldrassil send them to Alathea to undertake spiritual rites—such as Stars of Elune and Elune's Grace—marking their transition into mature servants of the goddess.",["al"]={"priest quests alathea","stars of elune quest"},["q"]="Why do night elf priests visit her specifically?"},{["a"]="Yes. While human and dwarven priests belong to the Church of the Holy Light, any Alliance priest visiting Darnassus can learn general spells from her, though she only administers kaldorei-specific racial trials to night elves.",["al"]={"can humans train with alathea","alathea dwarf priest"},["q"]="Does she train races other than night elves?"},{["a"]="While the priests of Stormwind and Ironforge invoke the ambient and philosophical Holy Light, Alathea and her sisters revere Elune as a living deity, wielding starlight and moonlit wards alongside curative magic.",["al"]={"elune vs holy light","night elf priest lore"},["q"]="How does her faith differ from human and dwarven priests?"}},["kw"]={"alathea","darnassus","elune","elune's grace","priest trainer","priestess alathea","stars of elune","temple of the moon"},["n"]="Priestess Alathea",["s"]="Priestess Alathea is a night elf priest trainer residing within the tranquil halls of the Temple of the Moon in Darnassus. Devoted to the Moon Goddess, she guides novitiates in the sacred arts and racial blessings bestowed by Elune. Her teachings help night elf practitioners attune their minds to defensive prayers and celestial magic.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Standing within the soaring silver heights of Darnassus's grandest sanctuary, Priestess Alathea serves the Sisterhood of Elune as an instructor and spiritual guide. As night elf initiates progress beyond the quiet boughs of Shadowglen, they are directed to the Temple of the Moon to deepen their covenant with the Goddess. Alathea stands among the priestesses ready to impart sacred knowledge to those who dedicate their lives to healing, warding, and divine light.",["t"]="Devotion in the Temple of the Moon"},{["b"]="Unlike priests of the Holy Light who draw strength strictly from human and dwarven traditions, kaldorei priests draw directly upon the grace of Elune. Alathea plays a key role in testing and granting blessings tailored to night elves, such as Stars of Elune and Elune's Grace. Through her guidance, acolytes learn how to weave starlight into shields of swiftness and defensive power to survive the growing perils facing Kalimdor.",["t"]="Blessings of the White Lady"}}}}}
t["npc:raene-wolfrunner"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,377,21.527.0,32.500.0,12.519.1,36.138.0,43.125.0,42.165.0,40.169.1,49.166.0,53.180.1",["h"]="ad99ab",["n"]="Raene Correlobo",["s"]="Raene Correlobo. Raene Correlobo es una consumada oficial centinela y cazadora apostada en el corazón de Astranaar, en Vallefresno. Acompañada por sus leales compañeros, un lobo y un sable de la noche, coordina las labores de defensa a lo largo del bosque frente a las fuerzas invasoras de la Horda y las tribus de fúrbolgs corrompidos. Actúa como un apoyo vital para los adalides de la Alianza que se esfuerzan por proteger la espesura sagrada. Raene Correlobo permanece vigilante en Astranaar junto a sus fieles compañeros: Korra, un sable de la noche, y Dagri, un lobo. Como oficial de las Centinelas, supervisa las patrullas por todo Vallefresno y coordina la información que llega más allá de sus fronteras, enviando exploradoras como Kaela Lanzasombra a regiones vecinas como Sierra Espolón. La devoción de Raene por los antiguos bosques es absoluta; ha afirmado que preferiría enfrentarse sola a las fuerzas de tala de la Horda antes que verlas talar y quemar la madera sagrada sin impedimento alguno.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,1,0,1},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Hunter"]="As a seasoned hunter who commands both a wolf and a saber cat, Raene represents the wilderness mastery and kinship with beasts prized by her class.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers arriving from Darkshore, Raene is the principal officer coordinating the military and ecological defense of Ashenvale.",["race:NightElf"]="Raene embodies the Sentinel dedication to Elune and Kalimdor's wilderness, refusing to allow the woodland sanctuaries of Ashenvale to be despoiled."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Raene is stationed in Astranaar, the central night elf town of Ashenvale. She stands ready outdoors, flanked by her two animal companions.",["al"]={"raene wolfrunner location","where is raene","raene astranaar spot"},["q"]="Where can Raene Wolfrunner be found?"},{["a"]="They are her trained hunting companions: a saber cat named Korra and a wolf named Dagri, who remain by her side in Astranaar.",["al"]={"raene wolfrunner pets","raene wolf and cat","raene companions"},["q"]="Who are the animals standing next to Raene?"},{["a"]="She acts as a ranking Sentinel officer in central Ashenvale, issuing orders to scouts, managing outposts, and coordinating tactical operations against local threats.",["al"]={"raene rank","is raene an officer","raene sentinel role"},["q"]="What is Raene's role within the Sentinels?"},{["a"]="Teronis was aiding the Sentinels by seeking a gemstone needed for Dartol's Rod. He was slain in the field, leading Raene to recover his remains and complete his mission.",["al"]={"who is teronis","raene friend teronis","teronis death"},["q"]="What happened to Raene's friend Teronis?"},{["a"]="Corrupted tribes like the Foulweald and Thistlefur have grown increasingly aggressive, ambushing travelers on forest roads and threatening the stability of Astranaar.",["al"]={"raene furbolg quest","why fight thistlefur","foulweald ashenvale problem"},["q"]="Why is Raene focusing so heavily on the furbolgs?"},{["a"]="The reconstructed rod allows an adventurer to temporarily adopt the form of a furbolg, opening communication with Krolg to target and vanquish the corrupt chieftain Ran Bloodtooth.",["al"]={"dartols rod purpose","what does dartols rod do","raenes cleansing rod"},["q"]="What is the purpose of Dartol's Rod in her questline?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","astranaar","dagri","dartol","korra","raene","sentinels","teronis","thistlefur","wolfrunner"},["n"]="Raene Wolfrunner",["s"]="Raene Wolfrunner is an accomplished Sentinel officer and hunter stationed at the heart of Astranaar in Ashenvale. Accompanied by her loyal wolf and saber cat companions, she coordinates defense efforts across the forest against encroaching Horde forces and corrupted furbolg tribes. She serves as a vital anchor for Alliance champions striving to protect the sacred wilderness.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Raene Wolfrunner stands watchful in Astranaar alongside her trusty saber cat Korra and wolf Dagri. As an officer among the Sentinels, she oversees patrols throughout Ashenvale and coordinates intelligence reaching beyond its borders, dispatching scouts like Kaela Shadowspear into neighboring regions such as the Stonetalon Mountains. Raene's devotion to the ancient woods is absolute; she has declared she would sooner face the Horde's lumbering forces alone than watch them hack and burn through the sacred timber unhindered.",["t"]="Defender of Astranaar"},{["b"]="Beyond the tensions with the Horde, Raene is deeply invested in addressing the dark taint sickening Ashenvale's native denizens. She directs campaigns against hostile furbolg tribes, including aggressive strikes against the Foulweald camps harassing travelers and targeted culls against rising Thistlefur leadership. Her subordinate scouts keep close watch over changing furbolg behavior, relying on Raene's steady command to protect local settlements and passing wayfarers from coordinated ambushes.",["t"]="Stemming the Forest's Corruption"},{["b"]="Raene's most personal crusade involves Dartol's Rod, an ancient relic tied to furbolg purification. Her longtime friend Teronis was slain while searching for the rod's missing gemstone, prompting Raene to order his body recovered and pledge to see his research fulfilled. Working in tandem with the dryad Shael'dryn, she helps champions assemble the relic, ultimately enabling an adventurer to assume furbolg guise, confer with chieftain Krolg, and defeat the tainted leader Ran Bloodtooth to purge the regional threat.",["t"]="Dartol's Rod"}}}}}
t["npc:rhahk-zor"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="9,243,23.412.0,16.365.0,17.234.0,50.231.0,37.203.0,44.169.0,67.221.0,40.202.0",["h"]="2fae72",["n"]="Rhahk'Zor",["s"]="Rhahk'Zor. Rhahk'Zor es un descomunal ogro que ejerce de capataz principal en Las Minas de la Muerte. Supervisa las obras de construcción subterráneas de Edwin VanCleef y mantiene a raya a los obreros y mineros Defias a base de pura fuerza bruta y una disciplina implacable. En las profundidades de las colinas onduladas de Páramos de Poniente, la Hermandad Defias ha transformado las minas de oro abandonadas de Arroyo de la Luna en una fortaleza subterránea. Coordinar esta descomunal construcción exige una disciplina férrea, un papel que desempeña el ogro Rhahk'Zor. Nombrado capataz principal, supervisa a las cuadrillas de excavación y a los peones, empujándolos a abrir túneles y ensamblar los proyectos secretos de VanCleef.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warrior"]="Facing Rhahk'Zor is a test of raw frontline endurance, pitted against a massive ogre swinging a sledgehammer that shatters stone and bone alike.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance adventurers pushing into Moonbrook, Rhahk'Zor is the first grim proof that the Defias Brotherhood has organized far beyond petty highway banditry into a heavily fortified army.",["profession:Mining"]="Rhahk'Zor drives his miners with crude brutality rather than respect for the veins of gold, churning Westfall's storied old mines into a rushed industrial war machine."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Rhahk'Zor is an ogre who acts as the primary foreman and enforcer for the Defias Brotherhood inside the Deadmines. He stands watch over the initial excavation tunnels, ensuring the workforce keeps digging without stepping out of line.",["al"]={"rhahkzor","who is the ogre boss in deadmines","deadmines first boss"},["q"]="Who is Rhahk'Zor?"},{["a"]="Edwin VanCleef's rebellion relies on whatever muscle and mercenary talent they can acquire. An ogre provides unmatched physical intimidation, making Rhahk'Zor an ideal taskmaster to drive the grueling labor of excavating the mines.",["al"]={"why is there an ogre in deadmines","rhahkzor defias"},["q"]="Why is an ogre working for the Defias Brotherhood?"},{["a"]="He serves as the head construction foreman. Rhahk'Zor supervises the miners, goblins, and Defias builders as they hollow out the caverns, maintain equipment, and build fortifications for the Brotherhood.",["al"]={"what does rhahkzor do","rhahkzor role"},["q"]="What is Rhahk'Zor's job in the mines?"},{["a"]="Rhahk'Zor guards the early quarry chambers of the Deadmines, standing past the initial miner tunnels and right before the heavy iron threshold known as Rhahk'Zor's Door.",["al"]={"rhahkzor location","where is rhahkzor"},["q"]="Where in the Deadmines is Rhahk'Zor located?"},{["a"]="Ogres once inhabited the Deadmines during the First War before being wiped out by Blackhand's Horde. Whether Rhahk'Zor is a lingering remnant of those earlier clans or simply a brute hired by VanCleef remains unconfirmed.",["al"]={"first war ogres deadmines","ogre lore deadmines"},["q"]="Does Rhahk'Zor have any connection to the ogres from the First War?"},{["a"]="Defeating Rhahk'Zor breaks the Defias hold on the outer quarry, clearing the way through the reinforced blast door he guards and allowing trespassers deeper into the clandestine shipyards and workshops.",["al"]={"rhahkzor door","after rhahkzor"},["q"]="What happens when Rhahk'Zor is defeated?"}},["kw"]={"deadmines","defias","foreman","hammer","ogre","rhahk'zor","rhahkzor","vancleef"},["n"]="Rhahk'Zor",["s"]="Rhahk'Zor is a hulking ogre serving as the head foreman within the Deadmines. Overseeing Edwin VanCleef's subterranean construction efforts, he keeps the Defias laborers and miners in line through sheer brute force and heavy-handed discipline.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Deep beneath the rolling hills of Westfall, the Defias Brotherhood has transformed the abandoned gold mines of Moonbrook into an underground fortress. Coordinating this sprawling construction requires harsh discipline, a role filled by the ogre Rhahk'Zor. Appointed as head foreman, he oversees the excavation crews and laborers, driving them forward to carve out tunnels and assemble VanCleef's secret projects.",["t"]="The Foreman of the Deep"},{["b"]="Rhahk'Zor maintains order through relentless muscle rather than careful engineering. Armed with an immense stone-headed hammer, his idea of workplace supervision is direct and unforgiving. Defias diggers and goblin engineers alike step lively around him, knowing that falling behind schedule or showing defiance invites a crushing blow from the towering taskmaster.",["t"]="Brute Motivation"}}}}}
t["npc:rorian-the-dayseeker"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="20,375,24.414.0,24.408.0,28.201.0,40.91.0,52.208.0,55.181.0,57.219.0,28.156.0",["h"]="bf534b",["n"]="Rorian el Buscadía",["s"]="Rorian el Buscadía. Rorian el Buscadía es una figura anciana de los cielonatos situada en Thendal, en la Isla de Zephras. Supervisa la iniciación de los jóvenes volantones mientras descubren su vocación, dan el paso a la madurez y se sintonizan con los elementos naturales de su tierra natal. Bajo su atenta guía, los recién llegados aprenden los fundamentos de la supervivencia, la tradición y el servicio a su comunidad. Dentro de los serenos confines de Thendal, en la Isla de Zephras, Rorian el Buscadía se erige como uno de los mentores principales para los jóvenes cielonatos. Venerado por su experiencia y serena sabiduría, Rorian guía a los jóvenes durante su crucial transición a la edad adulta. Bajo su instrucción, los iniciados emprenden su tradicional rito de iniciación, demostrando que están listos para defender y apoyar a su hogar insular.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Mage"]="Novice arcanists find an understanding guide in Rorian, who directs budding scholars of the arcane toward teachers capable of honing raw magical potential.",["class:Shaman"]="Rorian places heavy emphasis on the island's harmony, dispatching fledglings to soothe agitated elementals and connect with ancestral traditions.",["class:Warrior"]="Rorian recognizes the physical dedication of aspiring fighters, pointing aspiring warriors toward the mentors who teach discipline on the battlefield.",["race:Skyborne"]="For every fledgling Skyborne, Rorian the Dayseeker represents the first threshold of duty and tradition, guiding your transition into adulthood in Thendal Village."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Rorian the Dayseeker is an elder Skyborne leader found in Thendal Village on Zephras Isle. He serves as the primary mentor for novice adventurers and fledgling Skyborne embarking on their early trials.",["al"]={"who is rorian","rorian role","what does rorian do"},["q"]="Who is Rorian the Dayseeker?"},{["a"]="He is located in Thendal Village, the starting settlement for the Skyborne on Zephras Isle.",["al"]={"where is rorian","rorian location","find rorian"},["q"]="Where can Rorian the Dayseeker be found?"},{["a"]="Rorian oversees the initial rites of passage that mark a fledgling's transition into adulthood. He tests their mettle and attunement to island life before directing them outward to serve the wider settlement.",["al"]={"rorian coming of age","skyborne trial mentor"},["q"]="What is Rorian's role in the Skyborne coming of age?"},{["a"]="Once a novice proves their worth, Rorian advises them on where to pursue advanced training, offering guidance toward the paths of the warrior, hunter, rogue, mage, shaman, or druid.",["al"]={"class quests rorian","choosing a class with rorian"},["q"]="How does Rorian direct new trainees into their classes?"},{["a"]="The natural balance around Zephras Isle is vulnerable to agitation. Rorian tasks capable initiates with investigating and calming elemental unrest so that Thendal Village and the surrounding wildlands remain in harmony.",["al"]={"elemental unrest rorian","why fight elementals zephras"},["q"]="Why does Rorian send adventurers to deal with elementals?"},{["a"]="Aetheen of the Gales is an individual on Zephras Isle to whom Rorian directs fledglings as they progress through their island responsibilities and training.",["al"]={"aetheen rorian","aetheen of the gales"},["q"]="Who is Aetheen of the Gales?"}},["kw"]={"dayseeker","fledgling","mentor","rorian","skyborne","thendal","zephras"},["n"]="Rorian the Dayseeker",["s"]="Rorian the Dayseeker is an elder Skyborne figure situated in Thendal Village on Zephras Isle. He oversees the initiation of young fledglings as they discover their calling, step into maturity, and attune themselves to the natural elements of their homeland. Under his watchful guidance, newcomers learn the fundamentals of survival, tradition, and service to their community.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Within the serene confines of Thendal Village on Zephras Isle, Rorian the Dayseeker stands as one of the primary mentors for the fledgling Skyborne. Revered for his experience and calm wisdom, Rorian directs youth during their crucial transition into adulthood. It is under his instruction that initiates undertake their traditional rite of passage, marking their readiness to defend and support their island home.",["t"]="Elder of Thendal Village"},{["b"]="Beyond fundamental trials, Rorian points promising initiates toward specialized paths suited to their talents. Whether an aspiring warrior, hunter, rogue, mage, shaman, or druid, fledglings are directed by Rorian to dedicated trainers across the isle. He also alerts them to elemental disturbances disrupting the island's harmony, instilling an enduring duty to preserve balance across the windswept heights.",["t"]="Guiding the New Callings"}}}}}
t["npc:scarlet-commander-mograine"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="26,332,22.349.0,17.393.1,46.170.0,47.169.0,18.212.0,46.244.0,44.249.0,48.203.0",["h"]="81e4d2",["n"]="Comandante Escarlata Mograine",["s"]="Comandante Escarlata Mograine. El Comandante Escarlata Mograine ejerce como líder militar de la guarnición apostada en el interior de la Catedral del Monasterio Escarlata. Como ferviente paladín de La Cruzada Escarlata, defiende la capilla junto a la Alta Inquisidora Melenablanca. Tanto la Horda como la Alianza lo tienen como objetivo para desbaratar a los fanáticos que amenazan los Claros de Tirisfal y las tierras circundantes. Apostado en la imponente Capilla del Cruzado, en el corazón del Monasterio Escarlata, el Comandante Escarlata Mograine lidera la guarnición permanente de La Cruzada Escarlata. Utiliza el poder sagrado de un paladín con feroz entrega, valiéndose de la reprensión, escudos divinos y golpes aturdidores para destrozar a cualquiera que la Cruzada considere corrupto o impuro.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Paladin"]="Mograine embodies the tragic corruption of the paladin's calling, twisting holy vows of protection and righteousness into ruthless, unyielding zealotry.",["faction:Alliance"]="Though the Scarlet Crusade once shared common ground with the Alliance, leaders in Southshore and Stormwind recognize that fanatical commanders like Mograine have descended into violent madness.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, Commander Mograine represents the sharpest blade of the Scarlet Crusade, whose presence directly borders the Undercity and threatens their survival in Tirisfal."},["faq"]={{["a"]="He is located inside the Cathedral wing of the Scarlet Monastery in northeastern Tirisfal Glades. You will find him waiting before the altar within the Crusader's Chapel.",["al"]={"mograine location","where is mograine","scarlet monastery mograine room"},["q"]="Where can Scarlet Commander Mograine be found?"},{["a"]="He serves as the military commander of the Scarlet Crusade's forces garrisoned at the Monastery, directing its paladins and soldiers alongside High Inquisitor Whitemane.",["al"]={"who is commander mograine","mograine rank","what does mograine do"},["q"]="What is Mograine's role in the Scarlet Crusade?"},{["a"]="Mograine fights as a heavy melee paladin. He uses Hammer of Justice to stun his opponents, unleashes Crusader Strikes, protects himself with Retribution Aura, and relies on Divine Shield when pushed to the brink.",["al"]={"mograine abilities","mograine combat","how to fight mograine"},["q"]="How does he fight?"},{["a"]="Whitemane and Mograine share an intense bond and fight together as leaders of the Monastery. When Mograine falls in battle, Whitemane intervenes, puts their attackers to sleep with her magic, and raises Mograine back to life with full strength.",["al"]={"whitemane res mograine","does mograine revive","resurrect mograine"},["q"]="Why does High Inquisitor Whitemane revive him?"},{["a"]="The Scarlet Crusade views all outsiders—living or undead—as carriers of corruption. Both the Alliance and the Forsaken send champions to strike at the Cathedral and execute its leaders to neutralize the Crusade's fanatical presence in Lordaeron.",["al"]={"why kill mograine","scarlet commander quest","in the name of the light"},["q"]="Why are the Alliance and Horde fighting him?"},{["a"]="Yes, in a pinch. Besides Divine Shield and his melee attacks, he can call on Lay on Hands to restore himself to full health, and High Inquisitor Whitemane adds further healing once she enters the battle.",["al"]={"can mograine heal","mograine healing"},["q"]="Does Mograine heal himself during the encounter?"}},["kw"]={"cathedral","crusader's chapel","mograine","paladin","scarlet commander mograine","scarlet crusade","scarlet monastery","whitemane"},["n"]="Scarlet Commander Mograine",["s"]="Scarlet Commander Mograine serves as the military leader garrisoned inside the Cathedral of the Scarlet Monastery. A zealous paladin of the Scarlet Crusade, he defends the chapel alongside High Inquisitor Whitemane. Both the Horde and Alliance target him to disrupt the zealots threatening Tirisfal Glades and the surrounding lands.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Stationed within the grand Crusader's Chapel at the heart of the Scarlet Monastery, Scarlet Commander Mograine commands the standing garrison of the Scarlet Crusade. He wields the holy power of a paladin with ferocious dedication, relying on retribution, divine shields, and stunning blows to shatter any whom the Crusade deems corrupted or unclean.",["t"]="Defender of the Chapel"},{["b"]="Mograine's defense of the chapel is intrinsically tied to High Inquisitor Whitemane. Should an attacking force bring the Commander to his knees, Whitemane emerges from the rear sanctum to turn the tide. Calling upon the Holy Light, she incapacitates intruders in an instant and restores Mograine from death, forcing their foes to confront both commanders in a desperate, simultaneous struggle.",["t"]="A Miraculous Bond"}}}}}
t["npc:senani-thunderheart"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="19,369,22.405.0,23.346.0,27.202.0,37.103.0,27.231.0,48.148.0,60.163.0,46.176.0",["h"]="20840f",["n"]="Senani Truenozón",["s"]="Senani Truenozón. Senani Truenozón es una cazadora tauren apostada en el Puesto del Hachazo, en Vallefresno, justo al norte de Los Baldíos. Al servicio de la Horda, pone a prueba el valor de los viajeros que pasan por allí desafiándolos a perseguir a los feroces depredadores salvajes que merodean por el antiguo bosque. A través de sus pruebas, los cazadores demuestran su destreza mientras reducen el número de mortíferas bestias que rondan cerca del territorio de la Horda. Establecida en el campamento del Puesto del Hachazo, Senani Truenozón representa las tradiciones de caza de los tauren en medio de las arboledas sombrías de Vallefresno. Lejos de las llanuras abiertas de Mulgore, encomienda a los aventureros de la Horda poner a prueba sus habilidades de rastreo y combate contra las bestias alfa del bosque. Considera la caza tanto un desafío honorable como un ritual necesario para sobrevivir en una tierra indómita y disputada.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Hunter"]="Senani embodies the classic hunter's spirit, testing your tracking skills against Ashenvale's elusive beasts: Ursangous, Shadumbra, and Sharptalon.",["faction:Horde"]="Splintertree Post serves as the Horde's foothold in Ashenvale, where Senani helps Horde scouts prove their worth and secure the wilderness.",["race:Tauren"]="For tauren travelers, meeting Senani brings a reminder of the Earth Mother's trials, honoring the ancient balance between hunter and quarry even far from Mulgore."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Senani Thunderheart is a tauren huntress and quest giver located at Splintertree Post in Ashenvale. She serves the Horde by directing adventurers to hunt the most dangerous wildlife prowling the forest.",["al"]={"who is senani","senani thunderheart lore","silverwind refuge questgiver"},["q"]="Who is Senani Thunderheart?"},{["a"]="Senani is stationed at Splintertree Post, the Horde outpost in Ashenvale directly north of the Barrens.",["al"]={"senani location","where is senani","where is silverwind refuge"},["q"]="Where can I find Senani Thunderheart?"},{["a"]="The Ashenvale Hunt is a series of hunting challenges issued by Senani. Hunters are tasked with tracking down and slaying three legendary forest predators: Ursangous the bear, Shadumbra the nightsaber, and Sharptalon the hippogryph.",["al"]={"the ashenvale hunt","what does senani want","hunting quests ashenvale"},["q"]="What is the Ashenvale Hunt?"},{["a"]="She asks hunters to return with Ursangous's Paw, Shadumbra's Head, and Sharptalon's Claw to prove that all three formidable beasts have been bested.",["al"]={"hunt trophies","ashenvale hunt items","what does senani need"},["q"]="Which trophies does Senani require for the hunt?"},{["a"]="Not in her own tasks. Senani's charge is the Ashenvale Hunt; the Foulweald and other furbolg tribes are simply among the many dangers a hunter faces in the forest.",["al"]={"foulweald quest","king of the foulweald","senani furbolg"},["q"]="Does Senani have any connection to the furbolgs in the area?"},{["a"]="No, Senani is aligned directly with the Horde and the tauren tribes, approaching the woods from the perspective of a traditional hunter rather than a Cenarion druidic guardian.",["al"]={"is senani a druid","senani cenarion circle"},["q"]="Is Senani affiliated with the Cenarion Circle?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","ashenvale hunt","mystral lake","senani","shadumbra","sharptalon","thunderheart","ursangous"},["n"]="Senani Thunderheart",["s"]="Senani Thunderheart is a tauren huntress stationed at Splintertree Post in Ashenvale, just north of the Barrens. Serving the Horde, she tests the mettle of passing travelers by challenging them to pursue the fierce wild predators that roam the ancient forest. Through her trials, hunters prove their skill while thinning the deadly beasts prowling near Horde territory.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Found keeping camp at Splintertree Post, Senani Thunderheart represents the hunting traditions of the tauren amid the shadowed groves of Ashenvale. Far from the open plains of Mulgore, she directs Horde adventurers to test their tracking and combat prowess against the forest's apex beasts. She views the hunt as both an honorable challenge and a necessary ritual to survive in an untamed, contested land.",["t"]="The Master of the Hunt"},{["b"]="Senani oversees the traditional hunting trials of Ashenvale, directing hunters toward three notorious predators: the bear Ursangous, the cat Shadumbra, and the hippogryph Sharptalon. Claiming their tokens—a paw, a head, and a claw—is a rite of passage that demonstrates a hunter's respect for the land and dominion over its fiercest denizens.",["t"]="The Beasts of Ashenvale"}}}}}
t["npc:senir-whitebeard"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,377,19.432.0,22.434.0,24.191.0,32.239.0,52.235.0,46.205.0,36.221.0,28.179.0",["h"]="d9b2e8",["n"]="Senir Barbablanca",["s"]="Senir Barbablanca. Senir Barbablanca es un dignatario y agente de campo enano apostado a las afueras de la Destilería Cebatruenos en Kharanos. En calidad de enviado especial del Senado de Forjaz, tiene la misión de vigilar las crecientes amenazas que rodean Dun Morogh. Su cometido se centra en evaluar la ofensiva de los trols Peloescarcha y transmitir sus movimientos directamente a los líderes enanos. Aunque la mayoría de los viajeros visitan Kharanos por su animada posada y su famosa cerveza negra, Senir Barbablanca está aquí en misión oficial. Al ser un representante enviado directamente por el Senado de Forjaz, su presencia subraya la seriedad con la que los altos mandatarios se toman la desestabilización de Dun Morogh. Sirve como un puente esencial entre los exploradores locales que arrostran peligros en la frontera nevada y los legisladores que debaten directrices tras las puertas de piedra de la ciudad.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance recruits passing through Dun Morogh aid Senir to safeguard the heartland of Ironforge from being cut off by indigenous troll uprisings.",["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, Senir represents the bureaucratic yet essential connection between frontier defenders and the governing body in Ironforge."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Senir Whitebeard is an envoy sent by the Senate of Ironforge to Dun Morogh. He stands outside Kharanos gathering intelligence on regional threats, especially the local Frostmane troll tribes.",["al"]={"who is this dwarf","senir whitebeard lore","who is senir"},["q"]="Who is Senir Whitebeard?"},{["a"]="Senir is stationed in Kharanos to observe troll activity and coordinate scout reports. Because Kharanos is the crossroad of Dun Morogh, it serves as the ideal hub to receive field intelligence before relaying it to the Senate in Ironforge.",["al"]={"why is senir here","senir kharanos role","what does senir do"},["q"]="What is Senir doing in Kharanos?"},{["a"]="The Ironforge Senate requires reliable, firsthand field data to allocate resources and direct guards. Senir serves as an impartial official assessing whether the Frostmane threat warrants immediate military escalation from the capital.",["al"]={"why envoy","ironforge senate kharanos","senate business"},["q"]="Why does the Senate of Ironforge need an envoy here?"},{["a"]="His chief focus is the Frostmane troll incursions. The trolls have been pushing aggressively out of their camps into dwarf territory, culminating in direct threats against nearby settlements like Kharanos.",["al"]={"senir main problem","what threat is senir watching","senir trolls"},["q"]="What is Senir's primary concern in Dun Morogh?"},{["a"]="No, Senir functions as an administrator and intelligence gatherer. He depends on local scouts, Mountaineers, and passing adventurers to enter hostile sites like Frostmane Hold and retrieve critical reconnaissance for him.",["al"]={"does senir fight","is senir a warrior","senir combat"},["q"]="Does Senir fight the trolls himself?"},{["a"]="Once Senir has compiled field notes regarding troll positions and strengths, the finished reports are sent directly up the mountain road to the Senate and leadership in Ironforge.",["al"]={"where do reports go","senir reports destination","who gets the reports"},["q"]="Where do Senir's reports go?"}},["kw"]={"dun morogh","frostmane","ironforge","kharanos","reports","senate","senir","whitebeard"},["n"]="Senir Whitebeard",["s"]="Senir Whitebeard is a dwarven dignitary and field agent stationed outside the Thunderbrew Distillery in Kharanos. Serving as a special envoy from the Senate of Ironforge, he is tasked with monitoring the growing threats encircling Dun Morogh. His mission centers on evaluating the Frostmane troll offensive and reporting their movements directly back to the dwarven leadership.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While most travelers visit Kharanos for its bustling inn and famous stout, Senir Whitebeard is here on official business. As a representative sent directly by the Senate of Ironforge, his presence highlights how seriously the high halls take the destabilization of Dun Morogh. He serves as an essential bridge between local scouts facing danger on the snowy frontier and the legislators arguing policy behind the city's stone gates.",["t"]="Envoy of the Senate"},{["b"]="Senir's primary concern is the escalating aggression of the Frostmane trolls. Displaced and desperate in the frozen crags, the trolls have begun pushing dangerously close to dwarven settlements and roads. Rather than charging into battle himself, the venerable envoy gathers reconnaissance on troll positions, particularly around their stronghold, compiling meticulous reports so Ironforge's military commanders can strike decisively.",["t"]="Eyes on the Frostmanes"}}}}}
t["npc:shadow-priest-allister"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="22,262,24.298.0,29.332.0,17.407.0,30.172.0,40.123.0,49.198.0,29.191.0,32.183.0,66.194.0",["h"]="9ca880",["n"]="Sacerdote de las Sombras Allister",["s"]="Sacerdote de las Sombras Allister. El Sacerdote de las Sombras Allister es un sacerdote Renegado apostado en El Sepulcro, en el Bosque de Argénteos. Al frente de las labores tácticas y de inteligencia en la región, coordina operaciones para vigilar a los magos de Dalaran y proteger las fronteras de Lordaeron para la Dama Oscura. Operando desde El Sepulcro, el Sacerdote de las Sombras Allister dirige el reconocimiento de los Renegados por todo el Bosque de Argénteos. Desde este asentamiento central en una cripta, rastrea las amenazas cercanas, que abarcan desde humanos renegados e incursiones bestiales hasta las maquinaciones arcanas que se desarrollan cerca de la cúpula resplandeciente de Dalaran.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Priest"]="As the author of 'Holy Bologna', Allister represents the Forsaken perspective on the Cult of Forgotten Shadow and their disillusionment with the Light.",["faction:Horde"]="Allister works to secure Silverpine Forest, ensuring Horde allies have safe passage between Tirisfal Glades and lands to the south.",["race:Undead"]="Allister exemplifies the Forsaken's ruthless pragmatism, turning his back on former holy dogmas to safeguard his people against living enemies."},["faq"]={{["a"]="He is a Forsaken shadow priest stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest who coordinates surveillance and strikes against nearby threats, particularly Dalaran forces.",["al"]={"allister","shadow priest allister","who is allister silverpine"},["q"]="Who is Shadow Priest Allister?"},{["a"]="He resides in the Sepulcher, the primary Forsaken settlement located along the main road running through Silverpine Forest.",["al"]={"allister location","where is shadow priest allister","find allister"},["q"]="Where can I find Shadow Priest Allister?"},{["a"]="The Kirin Tor mages stationed at Ambermill pose a constant threat to Forsaken territory. Allister seeks to decrypt their communications, uncover their intentions, and keep their influence contained.",["al"]={"allister dalaran","why attack ambermill","dalaran threat silverpine"},["q"]="Why is Allister focused on Dalaran and Ambermill?"},{["a"]="Allister authored 'Holy Bologna: What the Light Won't Tell You', an irreverent and critical critique of the Holy Light that found its way across the sea to the ancient libraries of Dire Maul.",["al"]={"allister book","holy bologna","what the light wont tell you"},["q"]="What book did Allister write?"},{["a"]="He offers several intelligence-gathering missions around Silverpine Forest, including Border Crossings, Maps and Runes, Ambermill Investigations, and tasks confronting Dalaran agents.",["al"]={"allister quests","sepulcher shadow priest quests"},["q"]="What quests does Allister offer?"},{["a"]="Like many Forsaken priests who felt abandoned by the Holy Light upon their deaths, Allister turned to the shadows, finding power and resolve in a discipline that embraces their undead existence.",["al"]={"why shadow priest","forsaken shadow magic allister"},["q"]="Why does Allister practice Shadow magic instead of the Holy Light?"}},["kw"]={"allister","ambermill","dalaran","forsaken","holy bologna","sepulcher","shadow priest","silverpine"},["n"]="Shadow Priest Allister",["s"]="Shadow Priest Allister is a Forsaken priest stationed at the Sepulcher in Silverpine Forest. Overseeing intelligence and tactical efforts in the region, he coordinates operations to monitor Dalaran's wizards and secure the borders of Lordaeron for the Dark Lady.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Operating out of the Sepulcher, Shadow Priest Allister directs Forsaken reconnaissance throughout Silverpine Forest. From this central crypt settlement, he tracks nearby threats ranging from renegade humans and beastly incursions to the arcane machinations unfolding near Dalaran's shimmering dome.",["t"]="Watcher at the Sepulcher"},{["b"]="Allister's chief concern lies with the surviving mages of Dalaran, particularly those occupying Ambermill and probing across the borders. Unwilling to let the Kirin Tor entrench themselves in Forsaken lands, he dispatches agents to intercept Dalaran messengers, decipher arcane runes, and determine the wizards' long-term ambitions.",["t"]="Eyes on Ambermill and Dalaran"},{["b"]="Beyond his duties as a field strategist, Allister is a cynical philosopher of the shadow. He is the author of 'Holy Bologna: What the Light Won't Tell You'—a scathing treatise criticizing traditional holy doctrine. The text explores the harsh realities of undeath and how the Holy Light fails those discarded by life, a work that has somehow circulated as far afield as the ruins of Dire Maul in Kalimdor.",["t"]="Heretical Musings"}}}}}
t["npc:shadow-priest-sarvis"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="20,390,30.491.0,19.340.0,28.176.0,38.114.0,51.201.0",["h"]="170b4e",["n"]="Sacerdote de las Sombras Sarvis",["s"]="Sacerdote de las Sombras Sarvis. El Sacerdote de las Sombras Sarvis se encuentra en el interior de la capilla en ruinas de Camposanto, donde ejerce de guía principal para los Renegados recién despertados. Muestra a los nuevos cadáveres su cruda realidad, encomendándoles purgar a los no-muertos sin juicio y reunir información sobre las amenazas locales. Bajo el estandarte de Lady Sylvanas, Sarvis trabaja sin descanso para convertir a no-muertos desorientados en siervos disciplinados de los Renegados. En la sombría capilla de Camposanto, el Sacerdote de las Sombras Sarvis aguarda a quienes acaban de salir de la tumba. El despertar de un Renegado resulta chocante y aterrador, y muchos pierden de inmediato la cordura sumiéndose en el frenesí irracional o el abatimiento. Sarvis actúa como un ancla, otorgando un propósito a los recién levantados. Encarga a los nuevos reclutas abatir a los cadáveres renqueantes y sin juicio que vagan por el cementerio y les ordena proteger las fronteras de Camposanto frente al avance de la Plaga.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Priest"]="Sarvis exemplifies the Forsaken's embrace of shadow magic, serving as a dark mentor figure in a chapel stripped of Holy Light.",["race:Undead"]="Sarvis is one of the very first voices you hear after waking from the grave, setting you on your path to serve the Dark Lady."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Sarvis is a Forsaken shadow priest stationed in Deathknell. He guides freshly awakened undead, giving them their initial orders and helping secure the town against the Scourge.",["al"]={"sarvis","who is sarvis","deathknell priest"},["q"]="Who is Shadow Priest Sarvis?"},{["a"]="He is located inside the ruined church at the center of Deathknell, the Forsaken starting area in Tirisfal Glades.",["al"]={"sarvis location","where is sarvis","find sarvis"},["q"]="Where can I find Shadow Priest Sarvis?"},{["a"]="Not every corpse raised from the grave retains their free will and sanity. Those who succumb to madness are deemed a hazard to the settlement and must be destroyed before they endanger the living dead.",["al"]={"why kill mindless ones","the mindless ones"},["q"]="Why is Sarvis having players kill mindless zombies?"}},["kw"]={"deathknell","forsaken","novice elreth","sarvis","shadow priest sarvis","tirisfal glades"},["n"]="Shadow Priest Sarvis",["s"]="Shadow Priest Sarvis stands inside the ruined chapel of Deathknell, serving as one of the primary guides for newly awakened Forsaken. He introduces fresh corpses to their grim reality, directing them to purge mindless undead and gather intelligence on local threats. Under Lady Sylvanas's banner, Sarvis works tirelessly to shape bewildered undead into disciplined servants of the Forsaken.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Within the shadowy chapel of Deathknell, Shadow Priest Sarvis waits for those who have just clawed their way out of the grave. The awakening of a Forsaken soul is jarring and horrific, with many immediately losing their minds to mindless frenzy or despondency. Sarvis acts as an anchor, giving purpose to the newly risen. He assigns new recruits to put down the shambling, mindless corpses roaming the cemetery and directs them to secure Deathknell's borders against the encroaching Scourge.",["t"]="Shepherd of the Newly Awakened"},{["b"]="Beyond acclimating new recruits, Sarvis oversees crucial local defenses against lingering threats in Tirisfal Glades. He coordinates the containment of Scourge forces probing Deathknell's perimeter. By directing novices toward vital intelligence and martial trials, Sarvis ensures that the town remains a fortified bastion for the Forsaken.",["t"]="Securing Deathknell"}}}}}
t["npc:shenthul"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="8,270,17.430.0,18.476.0,16.496.1,16.128.0,26.121.0,52.142.0,44.199.0,44.206.0,40.145.0",["h"]="67dca3",["n"]="Shenthul",["s"]="Shenthul. Shenthul es un instructor de pícaros trol de la selva asentado en las sombrías profundidades subterráneas del Circo de las Sombras, en Orgrimmar. Como agente de Mano Destrozada, coordina operaciones de espionaje por todo Kalimdor e inicia a los pícaros novatos en las filas clandestinas de la hermandad. Oculto en las turbias profundidades del Circo de las Sombras, Shenthul ejerce como uno de los mentores de pícaros más destacados de la Horda. Mientras los guerreros y chamanes de la superficie marchan abiertamente por el polvo rojo de Durotar, Shenthul adiestra a quienes prefieren el sigilo, la emboscada y el subterfugio. Bajo su tutela, los iniciados dominan las técnicas de campo esenciales y las artes letales, aprendiendo a desenvolverse en la despiadada política y las duras tierras salvajes de Kalimdor.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="Shenthul is a primary mentor and handler for Horde rogues arriving in Orgrimmar, offering skill training, initiation trials, and covert assignments.",["faction:Horde"]="Operating beneath the surface of the capital, Shenthul directs the covert intelligence arm that protects the Horde from unseen internal and external threats.",["race:Troll"]="As a jungle troll embedded deeply in the traditionally orcish Shattered Hand, Shenthul demonstrates how Darkspear rogues have woven themselves into the Horde's highest levels of espionage."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Shenthul is a jungle troll rogue trainer and operative of the Shattered Hand stationed in the Cleft of Shadow beneath Orgrimmar.",["al"]={"shenthul role","who is shenthul","troll rogue trainer orgrimmar"},["q"]="Who is Shenthul?"},{["a"]="He can be found in the Cleft of Shadow, the subterranean cavern complex accessed through the darker tunnels of Orgrimmar.",["al"]={"shenthul location","where is shenthul","shenthul cleft of shadow"},["q"]="Where can I find Shenthul?"},{["a"]="Shenthul is a dedicated operative and recruiter for the Shattered Hand, the covert intelligence and assassin guild operating within the Horde.",["al"]={"shattered hand shenthul","is shenthul shattered hand","what faction is shenthul"},["q"]="What is Shenthul's connection to the Shattered Hand?"},{["a"]="Shenthul is loyal to the craft and security of the Horde, but maintains that the Order of the Shattered Hand existed before Thrall and will outlast his rule, seeing his guild as an eternal necessity.",["al"]={"shenthul thoughts on thrall","does shenthul like thrall","shenthul loyalty"},["q"]="What does Shenthul think of Warchief Thrall?"},{["a"]="He guides rogues through initiation trials, sends them on covert infiltration missions, and points them to the Venture Company's locked supply boxes in the Stonetalon Mountains to improve their lockpicking.",["al"]={"shenthul quests","rogue quests shenthul"},["q"]="What missions does Shenthul offer to rogues?"},{["a"]="Yes, during crucial field operations where rogues face lethal toxins, Shenthul directs agents to Hinott to ensure survival and ongoing fieldwork.",["al"]={"shenthul poison quest","hinott assistance shenthul"},["q"]="Does Shenthul assist with rogue poisons?"}},["kw"]={"cleft of shadow","jungle troll","orgrimmar","rogue trainer","shattered hand","shenthul","venture company","windshear crag"},["n"]="Shenthul",["s"]="Shenthul is a jungle troll rogue trainer based in the shadowy subterranean reaches of the Cleft of Shadow in Orgrimmar. As an operative of the Shattered Hand, he orchestrates espionage operations across Kalimdor and initiates rising rogues into the guild's covert ranks.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked away inside the murky depths of the Cleft of Shadow, Shenthul serves as one of the Horde's foremost rogue mentors. While the warriors and shamans above march openly across the red dust of Durotar, Shenthul trains those who prefer stealth, ambush, and subterfuge. Under his tutelage, initiates master essential fieldcraft and lethal arts, learning to operate within the unforgiving politics and harsh wilderness of Kalimdor.",["t"]="Eyes in the Chasm"},{["b"]="Shenthul represents the Shattered Hand, an order transformed from an old orcish clan into the Horde's intelligence network and secret service. He views the organization as a timeless, watchful veil blanketing Kalimdor—acting as investigator, judge, jury, and executioner. Fiercely pragmatic and independent of shifting political tides, Shenthul famously reminds outsiders that the Shattered Hand existed long before Warchief Thrall took power and will endure long after him.",["t"]="The Shattered Hand"},{["b"]="Beyond basic training, Shenthul coordinates delicate missions into contested territories. His assignments send operatives on perilous infiltration assignments, such as conducting deep-cover operations against hostile interests, practicing their lockpicking on the Venture Company's locked supply boxes around Windshear Crag, and testing recruits through demanding clandestine trials. When poisons strike his field agents, Shenthul ensures they secure remedies before fatal consequences take hold.",["t"]="Covert Fieldwork"}}}}}
t["npc:sneed"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="5,251,23.454.0,20.486.0,13.178.0,25.141.0,51.212.0,33.153.0,44.154.0,34.178.0",["h"]="757f98",["n"]="Sneed",["s"]="Sneed. Sneed es el maestro maderero goblin de la Hermandad Defias, apostado en lo profundo de Las Minas de la Muerte. Desde la cámara maderera conocida como Sala de los Mástiles, pilota una pesada trituradora de diseño propio para procesar madera destinada al coloso secreto de Edwin VanCleef. Aunque la Hermandad Defias nutre sus filas principales de canteros humanos marginados y peones comunes, la construcción de un buque de guerra acorazado requiere oficios especializados. Edwin VanCleef reclutó a Sneed específicamente por sus conocimientos de ingeniería y su implacable eficiencia goblin. Apostado en la Sala de los Mástiles junto a la red ferroviaria subterránea, Sneed supervisa la rápida tala, corte y moldeado de la madera necesaria para la estructura del colosal acorazado de VanCleef.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Taking down Sneed cripples the supply of timber heading toward the Ironclad Cove, striking a critical blow against the Defias Brotherhood's shipbuilding efforts.",["profession:Engineering"]="Sneed's customized shredder showcases classic goblin craftsmanship: devastatingly efficient, heavily armed, and pushed far past standard safety tolerances to maximize production speed.",["race:Gnome"]="Gnomish visitors to the Mast Room will find Sneed's machine a typical example of goblin ingenuity—loud, hazardous, and built without regard for operator comfort or structural longevity."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Sneed is a goblin engineer and lumbermaster employed by Edwin VanCleef. He is tasked with overseeing the processing of lumber inside the Deadmines to build the Defias juggernaut.",["al"]={"who is sneed","sneed lore","what is sneed"},["q"]="Who is Sneed?"},{["a"]="Sneed is located in the Mast Room, an industrial lumber mill chamber situated along the mining tracks inside the Deadmines beneath Moonbrook.",["al"]={"sneed location","where is sneed","sneed room"},["q"]="Where can Sneed be found?"},{["a"]="Edwin VanCleef needed specialized industrial knowledge and fast results to construct his secret warship. He hired mercenary goblins like Sneed who care little about politics or ethics as long as the coin is good.",["al"]={"why is sneed with defias","goblin in deadmines","why defias hire goblins"},["q"]="Why is a goblin working for the Defias Brotherhood?"},{["a"]="Sneed pilots Sneed's Shredder, a heavy, saw-wielding bipedal mechanical harvester that he built himself to harvest and slice timber at terrifying speeds.",["al"]={"sneed robot","sneed mech","sneed's shredder"},["q"]="What is Sneed piloting in battle?"},{["a"]="Destroying the shredder does not finish the fight. Sneed ejects from the smoking remains of the machine and continues fighting intruders directly on foot.",["al"]={"sneed phase 2","sneed out of shredder","does sneed die with shredder"},["q"]="What happens when his shredder is destroyed?"},{["a"]="The timber cut in Sneed's chamber is transported downstream to the Ironclad Cove, where the Brotherhood is assembling a massive warship intended to strike back against Stormwind.",["al"]={"why sneed cutting wood","mast room purpose","deadmines wood"},["q"]="What is Sneed building timber for?"}},["kw"]={"deadmines","edwin vancleef","goblin","juggernaut","lumbermaster","mast room","shredder","sneed","sneed's shredder"},["n"]="Sneed",["s"]="Sneed is the Defias Brotherhood's goblin lumbermaster stationed deep within the Deadmines. Operating from the lumber chamber known as the Mast Room, he pilots a heavy shredder of his own design to process timber for Edwin VanCleef's secret juggernaut.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While the Defias Brotherhood draws its core membership from disenfranchised human stonemasons and common laborers, building an ironclad warship requires specialist trades. Edwin VanCleef recruited Sneed specifically for his engineering know-how and ruthless goblin efficiency. Stationed in the Mast Room along the subterranean rail network, Sneed oversees the rapid felling, cutting, and shaping of timber needed to frame VanCleef's colossal dreadnaught.",["t"]="The Defias Lumbermaster"},{["b"]="Sneed's primary concern is cutting costs and meeting deadlined quotas, consequences be damned. To speed up the process, he commands the floor from inside a customized shredder equipped with oversized buzz saws. The deadly machine turns raw trunks into shipbuilding timber in seconds. If cornered by intruders, Sneed relies on the armor of his machine to grind them down, but he is more than willing to scramble out of the wreckage and fight with his bare hands if his contraption fails.",["t"]="Industrial Brutality"}}}}}
t["npc:sneed-s-shredder"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,266,17.397.0,16.336.0,51.272.0,44.224.0,53.197.0,54.166.0,46.197.0,24.139.0",["h"]="64587b",["n"]="Machacador de Sneed",["s"]="Machacador de Sneed. La Machacador de Sneed es una imponente cosechadora de madera mecanizada ubicada en lo más profundo de Las Minas de la Muerte. Pilotada por el capataz goblin Sneed, esta letal máquina actúa tanto de maquinaria industrial pesada para los carpinteros de ribera de Edwin VanCleef como de aterrador defensor perimetral. En la fundición dominada por goblins de Las Minas de la Muerte, las trituradoras mecánicas cumplen un doble propósito: procesar las ingentes cantidades de madera necesarias para el coloso oculto de Edwin VanCleef y servir como máquinas de choque blindadas contra los intrusos. Sneed, el supervisor de las obras madereras, maneja directamente esta bestia mecánica modificada, convirtiendo una sierra circular descomunal en un instrumento defensivo.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Eliminating Sneed and his machine cripples the lumber milling operations supporting Edwin VanCleef's secret war fleet.",["profession:Engineering"]="The shredder is a classic marvel of goblin mechanical design, though it remains vulnerable to the overrides of a Gnomish Universal Remote.",["race:Gnome"]="Shoni the Shilent of the Gnomeregan underground assault crew wants this goblin-built monster's power supply to drive the drills that could reopen the way to Gnomeregan."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Defias Brotherhood relies heavily on goblin machinery to carve through subterranean stone and process massive quantities of timber needed to construct their secret juggernaut. Sneed uses this shredder to mill wood and brutally enforce order over the underground works.",["al"]={"why is there a shredder in deadmines","shredder purpose deadmines"},["q"]="What is Sneed's Shredder used for in the Deadmines?"},{["a"]="When the shredder suffers critical mechanical failure, Sneed himself survives the wreckage. The goblin pilot emerges directly from the ruined vehicle, brandishing his own weapons and attacking intruders with fierce tenacity.",["al"]={"does sneed die with the shredder","sneed shredder phase 2"},["q"]="What happens when the shredder is destroyed?"},{["a"]="Edwin VanCleef hired goblin engineers, craftsmen, and mercenary laborers to oversee the complex mechanical operations beneath Westfall, including steam-powered forges, gun foundries, and woodmills.",["al"]={"defias goblins","why are goblins in deadmines"},["q"]="Why do the Defias Brotherhood have goblin technology?"},{["a"]="Clever inventors carrying a Gnomish Universal Remote can briefly override the shredder's control systems, temporarily wresting control of the machine away from Sneed.",["al"]={"control sneed shredder","gnomish universal remote sneed"},["q"]="Can the shredder be hacked or controlled by engineers?"},{["a"]="Yes. Its intact power supply, the Gnoam Sprecklesprocket, is sought by Shoni the Shilent in Stormwind, who needs it to power the gnomes' gyrodrillmatic excavationators for an assault on Gnomeregan.",["al"]={"sneed shredder quest item","what drops from sneed shredder"},["q"]="Does Sneed's Shredder carry anything valuable?"},{["a"]="The machine is commanded by Sneed, a seasoned goblin supervisor who directs the logging and carpentry operations deep within the Deadmines.",["al"]={"who drives sneed shredder","sneed pilot"},["q"]="Who pilots the shredder?"}},["kw"]={"buzzsaw","deadmines","defias","goblin","lumber","remote","shredder","sneed","vancleef"},["n"]="Sneed's Shredder",["s"]="Sneed's Shredder is an imposing mechanised lumber harvester stationed deep within the Deadmines. Piloted by the goblin taskmaster Sneed, this deadly machine acts as both heavy industrial machinery for Edwin VanCleef's shipwrights and a terrifying perimeter defender.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Within the goblin-dominated foundry of the Deadmines, mechanical shredders serve a dual purpose: processing vast amounts of timber and lumber required for Edwin VanCleef's hidden juggernaut, and serving as armored shock engines against intruders. Sneed, the overseer of the lumber works, operates this modified mechanical beast directly, turning an oversized buzzsaw into an instrument of defense.",["t"]="Industrial Terror"},{["b"]="Defeating the machine does not end the threat. Sneed perches inside an open cockpit above the spinning blades, relying on heavy iron plating and terrifying clatter to scatter his foes. Even when the machinery breaks down and the shredder collapses in a shower of sparks, Sneed leaps from the smoking wreckage to fight to the bitter end.",["t"]="A Deadly Cockpit"}}}}}
t["npc:sprite-jumpsprocket"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="19,421,21.472.0,26.482.0,27.123.0,37.128.0,38.145.0,47.218.0,50.141.0,32.219.0",["h"]="110d49",["n"]="Duendy Ruedadentada",["s"]="Duendy Ruedadentada. Duendy Ruedadentada es una aprendiz de ingeniera gnoma que reside actualmente en el concurrido Distrito de los Enanos de la Ciudad de Ventormenta. Como muchos gnomos que buscaron refugio tras la caída de Gnomeregan, se dedica a la artesanía técnica y a la innovación junto a sus compañeros manitas. Su presencia pone de manifiesto la próspera comunidad de artesanos enanos y gnomos que mantienen la capital abastecida de engranajes, artilugios y conocimientos mecánicos. En las calles cubiertas de hollín y los bulliciosos talleres del Distrito de los Enanos, gnomos y enanos trabajan codo con codo forjando metal y diseñando complejos artilugios. Duendy Ruedadentada ejerce como aprendiz de ingeniera en este vibrante núcleo. Tras haberse integrado en la capital del reino, los aprendices de manitas como Duendy perfeccionan su oficio bajo la tutela de maestros experimentados, aportando sus mentes inventivas a los mecanismos cotidianos y a las maravillas tecnológicas de la Alianza.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Her work in the Dwarven District illustrates the everyday cooperation between humans, dwarves, and gnomes supporting the capital's infrastructure.",["profession:Engineering"]="For budding tinkers, Sprite Jumpsprocket stands as a fellow student of sprockets, copper tubing, and volatile concoctions in Stormwind's most industrial enclave.",["race:Gnome"]="Sprite is a reminder of the perseverance of Gnomeregan's exiles, continuing their love of craft and mechanical mastery far from their lost homeland."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Sprite Jumpsprocket is a female gnome apprentice engineer living and working within the Dwarven District of Stormwind City.",["al"]={"sprite jumpsprocket","who is sprite","sprite jumpsprocket lore"},["q"]="Who is Sprite Jumpsprocket?"},{["a"]="She can be found in the Dwarven District of Stormwind City, surrounded by workshops, anvils, and fellow engineering enthusiasts.",["al"]={"sprite jumpsprocket location","where is sprite","find sprite jumpsprocket"},["q"]="Where can I find Sprite Jumpsprocket?"},{["a"]="Sprite is an apprentice engineer. She represents the ongoing presence of gnomish tinkerers honing their inventive crafts in the Alliance capital.",["al"]={"sprite jumpsprocket role","what does she do","sprite jumpsprocket purpose"},["q"]="What role does she serve in Stormwind?"},{["a"]="After the catastrophic fall of Gnomeregan, many gnomes sought refuge among their dwarven cousins in Ironforge and throughout human lands, particularly Stormwind City, where their industrial ingenuity is in high demand.",["al"]={"why gnomes in stormwind","gnomes dwarven district","gnome refugees"},["q"]="Why are gnomes like Sprite living in Stormwind?"},{["a"]="Sprite plays a minor role in the local neighborhood of the Dwarven District, mainly standing as part of the district's engineering community.",["al"]={"sprite jumpsprocket quest","quests for sprite"},["q"]="Is Sprite Jumpsprocket tied to any notable quests?"},{["a"]="While sometimes indexed near surrounding southern kingdoms records, Sprite is stationed squarely in the Dwarven District of Stormwind City, though engineering creations throughout the region often share gnomish designs.",["al"]={"sprite jumpsprocket westfall","westfall engineer"},["q"]="Is she associated with Westfall?"}},["kw"]={"apprentice","dwarven district","engineer","gnome","jumpsprocket","sprite jumpsprocket","stormwind","tinker"},["n"]="Sprite Jumpsprocket",["s"]="Sprite Jumpsprocket is an apprentice gnome engineer currently residing in the busy Dwarven District of Stormwind City. Like many gnomes who sought refuge following the fall of Gnomeregan, she pursues technical craft and innovation alongside her fellow tinkers. Her presence highlights the thriving community of dwarven and gnomish artisans who keep the capital city supplied with gears, gadgets, and mechanical expertise.",["sec"]={{["b"]="In the soot-covered streets and bustling workshops of the Dwarven District, gnomes and dwarves work shoulder-to-shoulder forging metal and designing intricate contraptions. Sprite Jumpsprocket serves as an apprentice engineer in this vibrant hub. Having integrated into the kingdom's capital, apprentice tinkers like Sprite hone their craft under experienced masters, contributing their inventive minds to the everyday mechanisms and technological marvels of the Alliance.",["t"]="A Tinker in Stormwind"},{["b"]="Following the devastating loss of Gnomeregan, displaced gnomes dispersed across Alliance lands, bringing their singular knack for tinkering, chemistry, and mechanics with them. In Stormwind City, gnomes found a welcoming sanctuary within the Dwarven District, where blast furnaces and workbenches are plentiful. Sprite Jumpsprocket represents this resilient, forward-looking spirit—determined to master the complex discipline of engineering despite the hardships faced by her kin.",["t"]="Gnomish Ingenuity in Exile"}}}}}
t["npc:sputtervalve"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="12,348,19.475.0,27.515.0,18.389.0,20.244.0,50.265.0,22.208.0,19.214.1,51.246.0,26.185.0",["h"]="4ee381",["n"]="Petardol",["s"]="Petardol. Petardol es un estresado ingeniero goblin afincado en la ciudad portuaria de Trinquete. Al servicio del Gremio de Manitas bajo las órdenes del Director Riddlevox, supervisa la investigación y el desarrollo regional de trituradoras bajo unos plazos corporativos asfixiantes. Para mantener su puesto, suele contratar a aventureros que lleven a cabo espionaje industrial contra sus rivales de Ventura y Cía. Operando desde Trinquete, Petardol responde ante el Director Riddlevox del Gremio de Manitas. Puesto a cargo del desarrollo de trituradoras, no tardó en descubrir que mantener el ritmo de la mecanización moderna es una tarea brutal. Ante una competencia feroz y un plazo implacable, Petardol se vio con muy pocos prototipos funcionales propios. En lugar de admitir el fracaso ante el Gremio, recurrió a la clásica solución goblin: robar diseños mejores a quienquiera que los hubiese construido primero.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,1,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Though Ratchet maintains neutrality, Sputtervalve relies heavily on Horde travelers crossing the Barrens to break Venture Company operations and smuggle machine parts.",["profession:Engineering"]="Sputtervalve represents goblin engineering's ruthless ethos: when innovation stalls, steal the schematics from the nearest competitor."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Sputtervalve is a goblin engineer affiliated with the Tinkers' Union based in Ratchet. Director Riddlevox tasked him with shredder research and development, leaving him scrambling to deliver results before his strict corporate deadlines expire.",["al"]={"who is sputtervalve","sputtervalve ratchet","sputtervalve lore"},["q"]="Who is Sputtervalve?"},{["a"]="The Venture Company developed cutting-edge shredders at the Sludge Fen featuring interchangeable hands and superior control grips. Unable to surpass their designs legitimately, Sputtervalve resorted to corporate espionage to 'borrow' their blueprints and machinery.",["al"]={"why attack venture co","sputtervalve sludge fen","sputtervalve venture company"},["q"]="Why is Sputtervalve targeting the Venture Company?"},{["a"]="A samophlange is an intricate mechanical component found within Venture Company shredders and control consoles. Sputtervalve hires adventurers to extract and examine it in hopes of mastering their technology.",["al"]={"what is a samophlange","samophlange quest","what does samophlange do"},["q"]="What is a samophlange?"},{["a"]="Wizzlecrank is an operative and associate sent by Sputtervalve into the Sludge Fen to steal shredder prototypes. His mission went sideways when he became trapped inside one of the machines, requiring an escort out.",["al"]={"wizzlecrank","who is wizzlecrank","sputtervalve partner"},["q"]="Who is Wizzlecrank?"},{["a"]="He does not study organic curiosities himself, but his familiarity with the Barrens makes him an ideal contact. When shown the shard recovered from the Wailing Caverns, he points adventurers toward the druids perched on the hills above the caves.",["al"]={"the glowing shard sputtervalve","glowing shard wailing caverns","shard quest ratchet"},["q"]="Why does Sputtervalve care about the Glowing Shard?"},{["a"]="Director Riddlevox is the high-ranking leader of the Tinkers' Union who placed Sputtervalve in charge of shredder innovation, holding him to strict and unforgiving production timelines.",["al"]={"riddlevox","director riddlevox","tinkers union boss"},["q"]="Who is Director Riddlevox?"}},["kw"]={"ratchet","riddlevox","samophlange","shredder","sludge fen","sputtervalve","tinkers union","venture company","wizzlecrank"},["n"]="Sputtervalve",["s"]="Sputtervalve is a stressed goblin engineer stationed in the port town of Ratchet. Serving the Tinkers' Union under Director Riddlevox, he oversees regional shredder research and development under crushing corporate deadlines. To keep his standing, he frequently hires adventurers to engage in industrial espionage against the rival Venture Company.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Operating out of Ratchet, Sputtervalve answers to Director Riddlevox of the Tinkers' Union. Put in charge of shredder development, he quickly discovered that keeping pace with modern mechanization is brutal work. Facing fierce competition and an unforgiving deadline, Sputtervalve found himself with few working prototypes of his own. Rather than admit failure to the Union, he turned toward the classic goblin solution: stealing better designs from whoever built them first.",["t"]="Industrial Pressure"},{["b"]="Sputtervalve's primary target is the Venture Company's drilling operation at the Sludge Fen to the northwest. Their latest shredder models boast interchangeable hands, refined control grips, and advanced internal mechanisms like the elusive samophlange. Desperate to crack their secrets, Sputtervalve dispatched his associate Wizzlecrank into the Fen for 'field research,' only for the operative to get trapped, forcing Sputtervalve to hire wandering mercenaries to recover stolen technology and rescue his partner.",["t"]="Eyes on the Venture Company"},{["b"]="Beyond his shredder dilemmas, Sputtervalve acts as a general point of contact for strange curiosities passing through the Barrens. When adventurers drag bizarre, corrupter-infused artifacts out of the Wailing Caverns—such as a glowing shard—Sputtervalve knows enough about the local landscape to direct them away from gadgetry and toward the isolated druids encamped above the caverns.",["t"]="A Fixer in Ratchet"}}}}}
t["npc:sten-stoutarm"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,292,26.364.0,22.403.0,21.189.0,43.240.0,34.244.0,52.160.0,30.185.0,63.192.0",["h"]="903334",["n"]="Sten Brazofuerte",["s"]="Sten Brazofuerte. Sten Brazofuerte es un práctico sastre y mensajero enano apostado frente a Yunquemar, en el Valle de Crestanevada. Encargado de mantener equipados a los nuevos reclutas y de gestionar los despachos locales, ayuda a garantizar que los montañeros noveles permanezcan abrigados, alimentados e informados a pesar de las duras condiciones de la montaña. Situado cerca del corazón del Valle de Crestanevada, Sten Brazofuerte es uno de los primeros rostros amables con los que se topan los nuevos reclutas enanos y gnomos frente a la taberna de Yunquemar. Con el valle aislado por las ventiscas invernales y los peligros invasores, Sten se encarga personalmente de equipar a los aprendices novatos con equipo resistente antes de que se congelen o se adentren sin preparación en la nieve acumulada.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Maintaining communication through Coldridge Pass is critical for Ironforge's training grounds, and Sten's mail network keeps the valley connected to the wider Alliance.",["race:Dwarf"]="Sten embodies the no-nonsense hospitality of Dun Morogh, making sure his kin are clad in thick leather and fed before sending them into the snow.",["race:Gnome"]="As gnomish refugees train alongside dwarves in Anvilmar, Sten treats them with the same practical expectations, dispatching them with mail and outfitting them for the elements."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Sten Stoutarm is a dwarven outfitter and messenger stationed outside Anvilmar in Coldridge Valley. He assists fresh recruits by supplying warm clothing and delegating local mail deliveries.",["al"]={"sten stoutarm","who is sten","anvilmar postman"},["q"]="Who is Sten Stoutarm?"},{["a"]="Sten serves as both a quartermaster and courier contact for Anvilmar. He collects local resources like wolf meat and pelts to craft protective gear for apprentices, while also routing correspondence and training memoranda across the valley.",["al"]={"sten job","what does sten do","sten role"},["q"]="What role does he play in Coldridge Valley?"},{["a"]="With Coldridge Pass endangered by troggs and winter weather, mail and supplies struggle to flow into the valley. Once messages make it through, Sten relies on dependable novices to deliver parcels and letters to residents such as Talin Keeneye.",["al"]={"why coldridge mail delivery","sten mail","coldridge valley mail delivery"},["q"]="Why does Sten need mail delivered?"},{["a"]="Sten takes a weary, unimpressed view of the pests infesting the surrounding hills, famously remarking that once you have seen one trogg, you have seen them all.",["al"]={"sten troggs","trogg quote","sten on troggs"},["q"]="What does Sten think about the troggs in the valley?"},{["a"]="Sten trades durable, warm gloves to passing adventurers in exchange for tough wolf meat, helping sustain the valley's defenders while outfitting them against the biting Dun Morogh cold.",["al"]={"dwarven outfitters quest","wolf meat quest","sten wolf meat"},["q"]="Why does he ask for wolf meat?"},{["a"]="They are sealed letters and training tokens dispatched from superiors across Ironforge and Dun Morogh, directing young apprentices to report to their respective class trainers inside Anvilmar.",["al"]={"consecrated rune","simple memorandum","sten notes"},["q"]="What are the runes and memoranda Sten gives to new adventurers?"}},["kw"]={"anvilmar","coldridge","dun morogh","mail","outfitter","sten","stoutarm","trogg"},["n"]="Sten Stoutarm",["s"]="Sten Stoutarm is a practical dwarven outfitter and courier stationed outside Anvilmar in Coldridge Valley. Responsible for keeping new recruits equipped and managing local dispatches, he helps ensure that novice mountaineers stay warm, fed, and informed despite the harsh mountain conditions.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Positioned near the heart of Coldridge Valley, Sten Stoutarm is one of the first friendly faces new dwarven and gnomish recruits encounter outside Anvilmar's tavern. With the valley isolated by winter blizzards and encroaching dangers, Sten takes it upon himself to outfit green apprentices with sturdy gear before they freeze or wander unprepared into the drifts.",["t"]="A Helping Hand in the Snow"},{["b"]="Beyond assembling winter outfitting from local wolf hides, Sten serves as an informal postmaster for Coldridge Valley. He handles messages passed through the treacherous Coldridge Pass and distributes official runes, memoranda, and orders to class trainers throughout the basin, ensuring novice warriors, priests, and mages get their instructions despite the hostile trogg presence blocking the tunnels.",["t"]="Keeping the Lines Open"}}}}}
t["npc:strahad-farsan"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,386,23.432.0,25.558.0,22.316.0,45.274.0,36.264.0,62.229.0,37.187.0,38.235.0",["h"]="54ae75",["n"]="Strahad Farsan",["s"]="Strahad Farsan. Strahad Farsan es un maestro brujo humano que habita en una apartada torre de piedra con vistas a Trinquete, en Los Baldíos. Renombrado más allá de las fronteras de las facciones, opera al margen de la política convencional de la Alianza y de la Horda, instruyendo a aspirantes a invocadores en las peligrosas artes de someter a demonios mayores. Practicantes de la magia vil tanto de Ventormenta como de Orgrimmar y Entrañas acuden en busca de su rigurosa tutela. Encaramada en los riscos situados sobre el puerto goblin de Trinquete, la torre de Strahad Farsan se erige apartada de los bulliciosos muelles comerciales. La neutralidad de Trinquete le otorga a Strahad la libertad necesaria para llevar a cabo peligrosas invocaciones demoníacas lejos de las miradas indiscretas de los magistrados de la Alianza o los chamanes de la Horda. Rodeado de sus acólitos, estudia los misterios más profundos del Vacío Abisal en relativo aislamiento, ajeno a las disputas territoriales menores.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warlock"]="Strahad is a pivotal mentor for intermediate summoners, guiding you through the harrowing rituals required to bind felhunters and summon steeds from the Nether.",["faction:Alliance"]="Sent by Gakin the Darkbinder from the crypts of the Slaughtered Lamb, Alliance warlocks travel to Kalimdor specifically to study under Strahad.",["faction:Horde"]="Despite being an Alliance-born human, Strahad remains open to dealing with Horde practitioners under the neutral aegis of Ratchet.",["race:Human"]="Strahad demonstrates that human masters of the dark arts operate far beyond the kingdom of Stormwind when seeking greater power."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Strahad Farsan is an accomplished human warlock and master trainer residing in a stone tower above Ratchet. He belongs to the inner circle of the prominent Stormwind warlock Gakin the Darkbinder, but his immense skill in demonic summoning makes him an authority sought by warlocks of both the Alliance and the Horde.",["al"]={"strahad lore","who is strahad","strahad farsan info"},["q"]="Who is Strahad Farsan?"},{["a"]="Ratchet is a neutral port run by the Steamwheedle Cartel, providing an ideal haven for dark spellcasters. Living on the bluffs allows Strahad to experiment with dangerous summoning rituals far from the restrictive laws of the Alliance and the watchful scrutiny of the Horde.",["al"]={"why is strahad in ratchet","human in the barrens","strahad location"},["q"]="Why is a human warlock living in the Barrens?"},{["a"]="Strahad's mastery over demonic entities transcends factional allegiance. Mentors in Orgrimmar and the Undercity acknowledge his expertise in binding complex demons, such as felhunters, and send their most promising pupils across the sea to learn directly from him.",["al"]={"horde visiting strahad","can horde talk to strahad","why do orcs go to strahad"},["q"]="Why do Horde warlocks visit Strahad?"},{["a"]="When Strahad first attempted to bind a felhunter, the ritual nearly cost him his life. He barely survived the confrontation, an experience that taught him the brutal precision required to subjugate such magic-consuming predators.",["al"]={"strahad felhunter encounter","strahad backstory felhunter"},["q"]="What happened to Strahad when he summoned his first felhunter?"},{["a"]="They share the uncommon surname Farsan, which strongly suggests a family connection, though Strahad remains focused entirely on his dark craft and reveals nothing about his familial ties.",["al"]={"godrick farsan connection","godrick farsan relative","is strahad related to godrick"},["q"]="Is Strahad related to Godrick Farsan?"},{["a"]="Strahad oversees several dedicated acolytes, including Magaz, Fenrick, and Wytula. They assist him with maintaining protective wards, preparing intricate summoning circles, and tending to the demanding rituals carried out at the tower.",["al"]={"strahad acolytes","acolytes in tower ratchet"},["q"]="Who are the acolytes around his tower?"}},["kw"]={"barrens","cabal","farsan","felhunter","gakin","ratchet","strahad","summoner","warlock"},["n"]="Strahad Farsan",["s"]="Strahad Farsan is a master human warlock who dwells in a secluded stone tower overlooking Ratchet in the Barrens. Renowned across faction lines, he operates outside conventional Alliance and Horde politics, training aspiring summoners in the dangerous arts of binding higher demons. Practitioners of fel magic from Stormwind, Orgrimmar, and the Undercity alike seek his severe guidance.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Perched on the bluffs above the goblin port of Ratchet, Strahad Farsan's tower stands apart from the bustling trade docks below. Ratchet's neutrality offers Strahad the freedom to conduct perilous demonic summonings away from the prying eyes of Alliance magistrates or Horde shamans. Surrounded by his acolytes, he studies the deeper mysteries of the Twisting Nether in relative seclusion, unbothered by petty territorial squabbles.",["t"]="The Tower Above Ratchet"},{["b"]="Strahad earned his formidable reputation through direct, deadly experience. When first binding a felhunter into service, he barely escaped with his life—an ordeal that left him both acutely cautious and unyielding in his expectations. Despite his human heritage, he has earned the respect of shadowy figures across Azeroth, including Gakin the Darkbinder in Stormwind and demonic scholars in the Undercity and Orgrimmar. Warlocks of any banner who wish to command creatures as volatile as felhunters or fiery steeds are inevitably directed to his doorstep.",["t"]="Master of Demonic Binding"}}}}}
t["npc:sylvanas-windrunner"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="19,463,26.512.0,20.567.0,27.271.0,51.301.0,47.285.0,32.262.0",["h"]="e80540",["n"]="Sylvanas Brisaveloz",["s"]="Sylvanas Brisaveloz. Lady Sylvanas Brisaveloz es la Reina Alma en Pena y gobernante suprema de los Renegados, y celebra audiencia en Entrañas, bajo las Ruinas de Lordaeron. Antaño la valiente General Forestal de Lunargenta, fue asesinada y alzada en la no-muerte por Arthas Menethil antes de liberarse del yugo del Rey Exánime. Ahora aliada con la Horda de Thrall por pura supervivencia mutua, está ferozmente dedicada a asegurar un futuro para sus no-muertos con libre albedrío y a cobrarse venganza contra la Plaga. En vida, Lady Sylvanas fue la célebre General Forestal de Lunargenta, al mando de la defensa de Quel'Thalas durante la Tercera Guerra. Cuando el príncipe Arthas Menethil marchó con la Plaga hacia el reino de los altos elfos para alcanzar la Fuente del Sol, Sylvanas luchó con ferocidad para frenar su avance. Frustrado por su resistencia, Arthas la asesinó, pero le negó una muerte limpia. Arrancó su alma de su cadáver y la transformó en una vengativa alma en pena, obligándola a servir a la Plaga y a colaborar en la matanza de su propio pueblo.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Though accepted into the Horde through the advocacy of Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem and Thrall's compassion, many orcs and trolls view Sylvanas and her court with lingering wariness.",["race:Undead"]="To the Forsaken, the Dark Lady is a liberator and protector, the solitary reason they possess free will and a fortified home rather than mindlessly serving the Scourge."},["faq"]={{["a"]="She is the sovereign leader of the Forsaken, holding court in the Royal Quarter of the Undercity. In life she was the elven Ranger-General of Quel'Thalas, but after being slain and raised by Arthas Menethil, she broke away from the Scourge to lead the free-willed undead.",["al"]={"banshee queen","who is the dark lady","lady sylvanas","undercity leader"},["q"]="Who is Sylvanas Windrunner?"},{["a"]="The Forsaken are reviled by the living nations of the Alliance, who see them only as monsters. Surrounded by the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade in Lordaeron, Sylvanas required strong allies to ensure her fledgling nation's survival, prompting her to petition Warchief Thrall for entry into the Horde.",["al"]={"why are undead in horde","forsaken horde alliance","sylvanas thrall pact"},["q"]="Why did Sylvanas align the Forsaken with the Horde?"},{["a"]="When the Lich King's psychic power began to bleed away during the aftermath of the Third War, his iron control over the Scourge fractured. Sylvanas was among the first powerful spirits to regain her autonomy, immediately reclaiming her mortal remains and turning her wrath upon Arthas.",["al"]={"how did sylvanas escape arthas","sylvanas free will","lich king control"},["q"]="How did Sylvanas break free from the Lich King?"},{["a"]="Above all else, Sylvanas seeks total retribution against Arthas Menethil and the Scourge for destroying her homeland and enslaving her soul. Concurrently, she strives to fortify the Undercity and carve out a secure, permanent haven for the Forsaken in Lordaeron.",["al"]={"what does sylvanas want","sylvanas motivation","dark lady goal"},["q"]="What is Sylvanas's primary goal?"}},["kw"]={"arthas","banshee queen","dark lady","forsaken","lordaeron","ranger-general","sylvanas","undercity","windrunner"},["n"]="Sylvanas Windrunner",["s"]="Lady Sylvanas Windrunner is the Banshee Queen and supreme ruler of the Forsaken, holding court in the Undercity beneath the ruins of Lordaeron. Once the brave Ranger-General of Silvermoon, she was slain and raised into undeath by Arthas Menethil before breaking free from the Lich King's grip. Now allied with Thrall's Horde out of mutual survival, she is fiercely dedicated to securing a future for her free-willed undead and exacting vengeance upon the Scourge.",["sec"]={{["b"]="In life, Lady Sylvanas was the celebrated Ranger-General of Silvermoon, commanding the defense of Quel'Thalas during the Third War. When Prince Arthas Menethil marched the Scourge into the high elven kingdom to reach the Sunwell, Sylvanas fought fiercely to delay his advance. Frustrated by her resistance, Arthas murdered her, but denied her a clean death. He ripped her soul from her corpse and twisted it into a vengeful banshee, forcing her to serve the Scourge and assist in the slaughter of her own people.",["t"]="Fall of the Ranger-General"},{["b"]="When the Lich King's magical grip fractured after the Third War, Sylvanas broke free of his dominion and repossessed her preserved body. Amassing other undead who had regained their free will, she overthrew the dreadlords occupying the ruins of Lordaeron, dubbed her people the Forsaken, and established the subterranean realm of the Undercity. Recognizing the precarious isolation of her people—threatened by Scourge remnants, zealous Scarlet crusaders, and suspicious human realms—she forged an uneasy alliance of convenience with Warchief Thrall and the Horde.",["t"]="Rise of the Forsaken"}}}}}
t["npc:tallonkai-swiftroot"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="19,238,22.323.0,21.396.0,27.158.0,37.113.0,31.211.0,44.242.0,33.210.0,52.159.0",["h"]="0dbca3",["n"]="Tallonkai Cruzarraíz",["s"]="Tallonkai Cruzarraíz. Tallonkai Cruzarraíz es un elfo de la noche residente de Dolanaar en Teldrassil. Preocupado por la incipiente corrupción que mancilla las grandes ramas, recluta a jóvenes aventureros para recuperar reliquias encantadas y frenar las viles fuerzas que asolan los bosques. Tallonkai Cruzarraíz habita en el asentamiento de las copas de Dolanaar, manteniendo un ojo vigilante sobre los bosques circundantes. Como muchos elfos de la noche que viven bajo las ramas del recién crecido Árbol del Mundo, está alarmado por la agitación antinatural de la fauna y las inquietantes sombras que se congregan en los confines de sus poblados.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Tallonkai's concerns center on relics that tether minds safely to the Emerald Dream, making his requests deeply relevant to druidic spiritual traditions.",["race:NightElf"]="Tallonkai Swiftroot represents the vigilance needed to protect Teldrassil during its vulnerable early years, asking young Kaldorei to purge corruption taking root in their new home."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Tallonkai Swiftroot is a night elf quest giver stationed in Dolanaar on the boughs of Teldrassil, dedicated to safeguarding the settlement from local threats.",["al"]={"who is tallonkai","tallonkai swiftroot","dolanaar questgiver"},["q"]="Who is Tallonkai Swiftroot?"},{["a"]="He is located in the town of Dolanaar, the central night elf village found just outside Shadowglen in Teldrassil.",["al"]={"tallonkai location","where is tallonkai","find tallonkai swiftroot"},["q"]="Where can I find Tallonkai Swiftroot?"},{["a"]="He asks travelers to retrieve the Emerald Dreamcatcher from the gnarlpine furbolgs, defeat the Gnarlpine furbolg Ferocitas the Dream Eater, and confront the warped gnarlpine threat in quests like Twisted Hatred.",["al"]={"tallonkai quests","what does tallonkai want"},["q"]="What tasks does Tallonkai give?"},{["a"]="Dreamcatchers are sacred night elf talismans tied to the Emerald Dream, used to ward against nightmares and dark visions. Their theft and corruption by hostile creatures poses a spiritual danger to the local druids and denizens of Teldrassil.",["al"]={"emerald dreamcatcher lore","why dreamcatchers"},["q"]="Why is he concerned about the dreamcatchers?"},{["a"]="Ferocitas the Dream Eater is the leader of a band of corrupted Gnarlpine mystics north of Starbreeze. He stole the emerald from Tallonkai's dreamcatcher and wears it on a necklace that glows green in the night.",["al"]={"who is ferocitas","ferocitas lore"},["q"]="Who is Ferocitas the Dream Eater?"},{["a"]="A growing sickness and unnatural corruption has seeped into Teldrassil, driving previously peaceful creatures like the gnarlpine furbolgs into violent madness.",["al"]={"why are furbolgs mad","twisted hatred lore"},["q"]="What is causing the unrest Tallonkai fights against?"}},["kw"]={"dolanaar","dreamcatcher","ferocitas","tallonkai swiftroot","teldrassil","twisted hatred"},["n"]="Tallonkai Swiftroot",["s"]="Tallonkai Swiftroot is a night elf resident of Dolanaar in Teldrassil. Concerned with the emerging corruption tainting the great boughs, he enlists young adventurers to recover enchanted relics and stem the foul forces plaguing the woods.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Dwelling in the canopy settlement of Dolanaar, Tallonkai Swiftroot keeps a watchful eye over the surrounding woods. Like many night elves living beneath the boughs of the newly grown World Tree, he is alarmed by the unnatural agitation of the wildlife and the unsettling shadows gathering at the edges of their settlements.",["t"]="A Sentinel of Dolanaar"},{["b"]="Tallonkai directs adventurers to confront foul entities disturbing Teldrassil's peace. His concerns include corrupted dream catchers crafted to protect sleeping druids, vicious gnarlpine furbolgs succumbing to a dark malaise, and the corrupted Gnarlpine mystics led by Ferocitas the Dream Eater. To Tallonkai, cleansing these disturbances is crucial to defending the fragile home of the Kaldorei.",["t"]="Threats in the Canopy"}}}}}
t["npc:taragaman-the-hungerer"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="22,358,15.413.0,12.450.1,45.187.0,63.230.0,39.244.0,29.144.0,34.179.0,35.180.0",["h"]="572291",["n"]="Taragaman el Hambriento",["s"]="Taragaman el Hambriento. Taragaman el Hambriento es un descomunal guardia vil que acecha en las cavernas incandescentes de Sima Ígnea, bajo Orgrimmar. Aunque muchos le temen como el amo demoníaco tras el culto Filoardiente, su presencia en las profundidades ardientes sirve a un propósito más oscuro y engañoso. La Horda busca su destrucción para purgar la corrupción demoníaca que envenena las entrañas de la ciudad. Merodeando entre los charcos de magma de Sima Ígnea, Taragaman el Hambriento representa una amenaza inmediata y aterradora para la seguridad de Orgrimmar. Para muchos exploradores y jóvenes guerreros enviados a la oscura sima, el guardia vil demoníaco parece ser el cabecilla principal de los cultores Filoardiente, sirviéndose de una fuerza infernal para doblegar a los débiles de espíritu y corromper los pasajes subterráneos bajo la fortaleza de Thrall.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warlock"]="While warlocks practice their dark arts within the Cleft of Shadow above, a wild and hostile felguard like Taragaman poses an untamed danger to the secrecy and safety of their hidden craft.",["class:Warrior"]="Facing Taragaman requires standing firm against crushing physical blows and avoiding being tossed into the surrounding lava by his brutal uppercuts.",["faction:Horde"]="For the young warriors and spellcasters of the Horde, slaying Taragaman in the depths beneath Orgrimmar is a critical proving ground to protect their capital from demonic corruption."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Taragaman is a felguard, a brutal demonic shock trooper of the Burning Legion. He wields heavy melee strikes and fiery magic to crush intruders within the magma caverns of Ragefire Chasm.",["al"]={"what race is taragaman","taragaman demon type","is taragaman a demon"},["q"]="What kind of demon is Taragaman the Hungerer?"},{["a"]="He is widely believed to be. Taragaman is the most fearsome demonic power in Ragefire Chasm, and the Horde's young defenders are sent to slay him as the cult's master, though the chasm may hold more secrets than a single felguard.",["al"]={"who leads searing blade","is taragaman in charge","taragaman cult leader"},["q"]="Is Taragaman the Hungerer the leader of the Searing Blade cult?"},{["a"]="The Horde cannot allow an active demonic presence to fester beneath their capital city. Taragaman's infernal corruption threatens to poison Orgrimmar from within, and eliminating him is vital to securing the cavern passages beneath the streets.",["al"]={"why kill taragaman","slaying the beast quest lore","taragaman orgrimmar threat"},["q"]="Why does the Horde want Taragaman dead?"},{["a"]="Taragaman resides deep within Ragefire Chasm, located in the subterranean volcanic tunnels accessible from the Cleft of Shadow inside Orgrimmar.",["al"]={"taragaman location","where is taragaman","taragaman ragefire chasm"},["q"]="Where can Taragaman be found?"},{["a"]="Victorious adventurers carve out Taragaman the Hungerer's Heart as proof of the beast's demise to complete the task of clearing out the demonic vanguard festering below Orgrimmar.",["al"]={"taragaman heart","heart of taragaman","slaying the beast heart"},["q"]="What happens to Taragaman's heart?"},{["a"]="Taragaman relies on devastating physical attacks, a powerful uppercut that knocks foes through the air, and occasional bursts of Fire Nova that scorch anyone standing close to him.",["al"]={"taragaman abilities","taragaman boss fight","taragaman mechanics"},["q"]="How does Taragaman fight in combat?"}},["kw"]={"bazzalan","demon","felguard","hungerer","jergosh","orgrimmar","ragefire chasm","searing blade","taragaman"},["n"]="Taragaman the Hungerer",["s"]="Taragaman the Hungerer is a hulking felguard lurking within the molten caverns of Ragefire Chasm beneath Orgrimmar. While widely feared as the demonic master behind the Searing Blade cult, his presence in the fiery depths serves a darker, more deceptive purpose. The Horde seeks his destruction to eliminate the demonic taint poisoning the city's underbelly.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Prowling amidst the magma pools of Ragefire Chasm, Taragaman the Hungerer represents an immediate and terrifying threat to the safety of Orgrimmar. For many scouts and young warriors sent into the dark chasm, the demonic felguard appears to be the central ringleader of the Searing Blade cultists, wielding infernal strength to bend the weak-willed and corrupt the subterranean passages beneath Thrall's fortress.",["t"]="The Beast Below"},{["b"]="Despite his commanding demeanor and devastating brutality, Taragaman is not the mastermind directing the Searing Blade. True leadership of the cult rests in the shadows with the satyr Bazzalan and the warlock Jergosh the Invoker. To these calculating schemers, the towering felguard is little more than expendable bait—a monstrous distraction designed to draw aspiring Horde defenders into the searing volcanic depths where they can be slaughtered.",["t"]="Lethal Decoy"}}}}}
t["npc:targorr-the-dread"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,376,23.455.0,14.463.0,21.464.0,25.214.0,49.243.0,49.284.0,27.230.0,27.130.0,33.178.0",["h"]="7f734b",["n"]="Targor el Pavoroso",["s"]="Targor el Pavoroso. Targor el Pavoroso es un infame verdugo orco Roca Negra encarcelado en las profundidades de las Mazmorras de Ventormenta. Conocido por sus brutales torturas a los soldados capturados de Ventormenta, su ejecución se retrasó indefinidamente debido a la incompetencia y la corrupción burocráticas. Cuando las Mazmorras estallaron en una revuelta liderada por la Hermandad Defias, Targor se liberó y se alió con los convictos amotinados. Antes de su captura, Targor el Pavoroso ejerció como verdugo supremo del clan Roca Negra bajo las órdenes del Señor de la guerra Gath'Ilzogg. Operando desde las ruinas ocupadas en Crestagrana, su crueldad destacó por ser excepcionalmente salvaje incluso para los violentos estándares de la Horda Oscura. Los guardias y milicianos de Ventormenta que luchaban por defender las tierras fronterizas fueron sometidos a tormentos agonizantes y a una muerte lenta a sus manos, convirtiendo su nombre en uno de los más aborrecidos del reino.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Putting down Targorr within the rioting Stockade brings long-overdue justice to the fallen defenders of Lakeshire and helps contain the chaos beneath the capital.",["race:Human"]="For humans of Stormwind—particularly those with ties to Redridge—Targorr embodies the terrible cost of the kingdom's bureaucratic failures and the ongoing threat of the Blackrock orcs."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Targorr the Dread is a Blackrock orc who served as the supreme executioner under Warlord Gath'Ilzogg. Notorious for torturing captured Stormwind soldiers, he was caught and imprisoned inside the Stormwind Stockade.",["al"]={"who is targorr","targorr lore","stockade orc boss"},["q"]="Who is Targorr the Dread?"},{["a"]="Although Targorr was captured and scheduled to face justice, Stormwind's inefficient, bloated, and corrupt legal administration dragged out the process. His execution was delayed by endless bureaucratic red tape until the prison riots erupted.",["al"]={"why wasn't he killed","why is targorr alive","stormwind corruption"},["q"]="Why wasn't Targorr executed when he was captured?"},{["a"]="Targorr does not share the Defias Brotherhood's political grievances, but during the chaos of the prison uprising, convicts of all stripes united against their jailers. He allied with the rioters simply to secure his freedom and slaughter any guards or adventurers who cross his path.",["al"]={"why defias working with orcs","targorr defias ally","stockade orcs"},["q"]="Why is an orc allied with the Defias Brotherhood?"},{["a"]="Guard Berton, stationed at Lakeshire in Redridge, offers a bounty for Targorr's severed head. The people of Lakeshire suffered extensively under Targorr's cruelty and want to see the execution Stormwind's courts failed to deliver.",["al"]={"who gives the targorr quest","guard berton targorr","targorr bounty"},["q"]="Who wants Targorr dead now?"},{["a"]="Targorr is located inside the Stormwind Stockade instance, holed up in one of the rear cellblocks alongside other rioting inmates.",["al"]={"where is targorr","targorr location","stockade room"},["q"]="Where can Targorr be found?"},{["a"]="Targorr belongs to the Blackrock orcs, part of the rogue Dark Horde remnants operating out of the Redridge Mountains and Blackrock Spire, rather than the New Horde led by Thrall.",["al"]={"targorr clan","is targorr horde","blackrock targorr"},["q"]="What clan does Targorr belong to?"}},["kw"]={"berton","blackrock","dread","executioner","gath'ilzogg","lakeshire","stockade","targorr"},["n"]="Targorr the Dread",["s"]="Targorr the Dread is an infamous Blackrock orc executioner imprisoned deep within the Stormwind Stockade. Known for his brutal tortures of captured Stormwind soldiers, his execution was indefinitely delayed by bureaucratic incompetence and corruption. When the Stockade erupted into revolt under the Defias Brotherhood, Targorr broke free and allied with the rioting convicts.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before his capture, Targorr the Dread served as the supreme executioner for the Blackrock clan under Warlord Gath'Ilzogg. Operating out of the occupied ruins in Redridge, his cruelty stood out as exceptionally savage even by the violent standards of the Dark Horde. Stormwind guards and militiamen who fought to defend the borderlands were subjected to agonizing torment and slow death at his hands, making his name one of the most reviled in the kingdom.",["t"]="The Butcher of Redridge"},{["b"]="When Alliance forces finally managed to capture Targorr alive, he was brought in chains to the capital and locked inside the high-security Stockade to await execution. However, the rot within Stormwind's judicial and political bureaucracy stalled the proceedings. Paralyzed by graft, endless paperwork, and neglect, the courts failed to deliver the death sentence he had earned, leaving a bloodthirsty war criminal sitting in a cell beneath the heart of the city.",["t"]="Justice Denied"},{["b"]="When the Defias Brotherhood staged their violent prison break, Targorr saw his opportunity. Breaking free from his cell, the ruthless orc threw his lot in with the Defias rioters, turning his cellblock into a slaughterhouse. With the prison entirely out of Warden Thelwater's control, towns like Lakeshire—still nursing the bitter wounds Targorr inflicted on their defenders—seek adventurers willing to venture into the riots and bring back the butcher's head.",["t"]="Uprising in the Cells"}}}}}
t["npc:tavernkeep-smitts"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,318,18.511.0,21.474.1,18.433.1,35.138.0,47.323.1,36.276.1,40.201.0,53.222.0,47.118.0",["h"]="bf6a86",["n"]="Tabernero Smitts",["s"]="Tabernero Smitts. El Tabernero Smitts es el camarero del Mesón del Cuervo Escarlata en Villa Oscura. Al regentar el centro social de Bosque del Ocaso, Smitts posee un conocimiento enciclopédico de los cotilleos del pueblo y de las tragedias locales sin resolver. Su prodigiosa memoria y su mirada atenta lo convierten en un contacto de valor incalculable para cualquiera que investigue la oscura historia de la región. Tras la barra del Mesón del Cuervo Escarlata, el Tabernero Smitts ofrece el calor del fuego y bebida a viajeros agotados, vecinos del pueblo y nerviosos guardias de la Guardia Nocturna que desafían los peligros de Bosque del Ocaso. Al ser una de las figuras públicas más veteranas del pueblo, Smitts se entera de cada rumor que se filtra a través de la penumbra. Mientras otros lugareños se encogen tras contraventanas atrancadas, Smitts vigila con ojo pragmático y observador a todo el que cruza su puerta, atento a conductas inusuales, huidas apresuradas y clientes extraños.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,1,1,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="Rogues investigating cold cases and shadowy figures will find Smitts an ideal informant, as he notices what patrons write, when they panic, and what they leave behind.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers stepping out of the shadowed woods, Smitts provides not just shelter and drinks, but essential local intelligence regarding the threats haunting Duskwood."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Smitts stands behind the counter on the ground floor of the Scarlet Raven Tavern, the central inn located on the town square in Darkshire.",["al"]={"smitts location","where is tavernkeep smitts","scarlet raven barkeep"},["q"]="Where can I find Tavernkeep Smitts?"},{["a"]="Years ago, Smitts accompanied Marshal Haggard to investigate the slaughter of visiting nobles. Smitts discovered muddy, torn pages at the scene, which he preserved. If presented with new evidence linking Stalvan to the crime, Smitts hands over the muddy journal pages so they can be delivered to Commander Althea Ebonlocke.",["al"]={"smitts stalvan","stalvan legend smitts","muddy pages stalvan"},["q"]="What does Smitts know about Stalvan Mistmantle?"},{["a"]="Jitters spent time staying at the Scarlet Raven Tavern, where Smitts observed him frantically writing in a journal before fleeing in terror. When you bring Jitters's journal back to the tavern, Smitts identifies it and directs you toward Raven Hill Cemetery to track him down.",["al"]={"smitts jitters","jitters journal smitts","inquire at the inn smitts"},["q"]="What does Smitts know about Jitters?"},{["a"]="Smitts is involved in procuring components for local concoctions, including sending adventurers into the cursed wilds for Rot Blossoms to brew a potent local mixture known colloquially as Zombie Juice.",["al"]={"zombie juice","smitts rot blossoms","smitts brew"},["q"]="What drinks does Smitts brew or request?"},{["a"]="Marshal Haggard is an old veteran of the Stormwind Guard who lives in a secluded cottage in the hills. He and Smitts worked together years ago to investigate the grisly noble murders, forming a bond over the unsolved case.",["al"]={"smitts haggard","haggard connection"},["q"]="Who is Marshal Haggard, and how does Smitts know him?"},{["a"]="None that anyone speaks of. Smitts keeps the Scarlet Raven on his own, and no relatives of his are known in Darkshire.",["al"]={"smitts relatives","mary smitts"},["q"]="Does Smitts have any known family in Darkshire?"}},["kw"]={"darkshire","duskwood","haggard","jitters","scarlet raven","smitts","stalvan","tavernkeep","zombie juice"},["n"]="Tavernkeep Smitts",["s"]="Tavernkeep Smitts is the barkeep of the Scarlet Raven Tavern in Darkshire. Operating at the social center of Duskwood, Smitts possesses an encyclopedic knowledge of town gossip and unsolved local tragedies. His long memory and keen eye make him an invaluable contact for anyone investigating the region's dark history.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Behind the bar of the Scarlet Raven Tavern, Tavernkeep Smitts offers warm hearth fires and drink to the weary travelers, local townspeople, and nervous Night Watch guards braving Duskwood's perils. As one of the longest-standing public faces in town, Smitts hears every rumor that filters through the gloom. While other townsfolk shrink behind locked shutters, Smitts maintains a pragmatic, observant eye on everyone who passes through his door, noting unusual behavior, hurried departures, and strange patrons.",["t"]="Heart of Darkshire"},{["b"]="Smitts has spent years quietly tracking the legend of Stalvan Mistmantle. When a visiting family of Stormwind nobles was butchered years ago, Smitts joined Marshal Haggard to examine the scene of the slaughter. Smitts recovered torn, muddy journal pages from the carnage, but investigators were never able to formally connect the handwriting to Stalvan at the time. Smitts held onto those faded scraps for years, convinced that the grim truth would eventually come to light.",["t"]="The Memory of Stalvan"},{["b"]="Smitts's attentiveness extends to contemporary threats as well. When the terrified hermit Jitters took refuge in the Scarlet Raven, Smitts watched him scribbling feverishly into a personal diary before fleeing the tavern in blind panic. When an investigator recovers the abandoned journal, Smitts readily recognizes the book and points the tracker toward Raven Hill, aiding the effort to unravel the cursed events plaguing the woods.",["t"]="The Shadowy Patron"}}}}}
t["npc:telf-joolam"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="11,212,19.360.0,16.337.0,19.152.0,31.114.0,50.198.0,36.166.0,46.198.0,50.154.0",["h"]="5563f8",["n"]="Telf Joolam",["s"]="Telf Joolam. Telf Joolam es un chamán trol de la jungla de Lanza Negra que custodia el Santuario de la Llama Latente. Guía a los iniciados de la Horda a través de las pruebas necesarias para comulgar con el volátil elemento del fuego y dominarlo. Encaramado entre los riscos que dominan las tierras fronterizas, Telf Joolam cuida del Santuario de la Llama Latente. A diferencia de la serena certeza de la tierra o la paciente profundidad del agua, los espíritus ígneos exigen una disciplina rigurosa y una concentración inquebrantable. Telf ejerce como maestro de pruebas, preparando a los jóvenes chamanes para demostrar su valía ante las ascuas salvajes antes de ser consumidos por ellas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Shaman"]="Telf Joolam is a key figure along your spiritual path, guiding you through the trials of the Fire Sapta to master your Fire Totem.",["faction:Horde"]="By safeguarding sacred elemental shrines throughout the borderlands, elders like Telf strengthen the spiritual backbone of the new Horde.",["race:Troll"]="Seeing a Darkspear elder keeper guiding initiates demonstrates how deeply troll spirituality has interwoven with the Horde's shamanic revival."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Telf Joolam is a Darkspear troll shaman serving as the keeper of the Shrine of the Dormant Flame. He mentors young shamans seeking to commune with fire.",["al"]={"telf joolam","who is telf","shrine of dormant flame troll"},["q"]="Who is Telf Joolam?"},{["a"]="He resides at the Shrine of the Dormant Flame, nestled high along the rocky ridge between Durotar and the Barrens.",["al"]={"telf joolam location","where is telf","how to find telf joolam"},["q"]="Where can Telf Joolam be found?"},{["a"]="The Fire Sapta is a specially brewed draught that opens an initiate's spiritual vision, allowing them to perceive and speak with elemental fire spirits that are otherwise invisible to mortal senses.",["al"]={"what is fire sapta","fire sapta use","why drink sapta"},["q"]="What is the purpose of the Fire Sapta he asks for?"},{["a"]="He specializes in the element of fire, testing shamans to ensure they possess the strength and will to control flame without falling victim to its destructive nature.",["al"]={"what element does telf teach","telf joolam element","fire totem quest guy"},["q"]="What element does Telf Joolam teach?"},{["a"]="Since joining Thrall's Horde, many Darkspear trolls have embraced the spiritual ways of shamanism alongside the orcs and tauren, with experienced practitioners like Telf guiding the next generation.",["al"]={"why troll shaman","darkspear shamanism"},["q"]="Why is a troll overseeing shamanic rites here?"},{["a"]="After proving mastery over the flame spirits upon the nearby peak, initiates gain the knowledge and blessing required to forge their permanent Fire Totem.",["al"]={"call of fire reward","what does telf give you"},["q"]="What happens after completing Telf Joolam's tasks?"}},["kw"]={"barrens","call of fire","darkspear","durotar","fire sapta","shaman","shrine of the dormant flame","telf joolam"},["n"]="Telf Joolam",["s"]="Telf Joolam is a Darkspear jungle troll shaman watching over the Shrine of the Dormant Flame. He guides initiates of the Horde through the trials required to commune with and command the volatile element of fire.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Perched among the crags overlooking the borderlands, Telf Joolam tends the Shrine of the Dormant Flame. Unlike the calm certainty of earth or the patient depth of water, the fiery spirits require sharp discipline and unwavering focus. Telf acts as a trialmaster, preparing young shamans to prove their worth to the wild embers before they are consumed by them.",["t"]="Keeper of the Flame"},{["b"]="Under Telf's direction, initiates brew and drink a ritual Fire Sapta to grant their mortal eyes sight into the unseen elemental planes. He directs supplicants up into the rocky summits to confront burning spirits directly, ensuring that every shaman who earns the flame carries respect for its ravenous hunger rather than reckless pride.",["t"]="The Path of Fire"}}}}}
t["npc:terenthis"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="9,326,23.437.0,20.412.1,17.132.0,30.162.0,46.144.0,43.136.0,46.181.0,46.160.0",["h"]="3046fb",["n"]="Terenthis",["s"]="Terenthis. Terenthis es un elfo de la noche druida apostado en el asentamiento costero de Auberdine. En representación del Círculo Cenarion, investiga la alarmante corrupción que se propaga por Costa Oscura y Teldrassil. Recluta a viajeros competentes para evaluar las crecientes amenazas a lo largo de la costa y ayudar a los aliados locales atrapados por la fauna corrupta. Enviado a Auberdine por el Círculo Cenarion, Terenthis se centra en rastrear la propagación del Musgovil y otras fuerzas corruptoras que se filtran en Costa Oscura desde Teldrassil. Los elfos de la noche ven esta plaga insidiosa con gran preocupación, temiendo que el equilibrio natural del norte de Kalimdor pueda quebrarse por completo si no se ataja. Terenthis trabaja para descubrir las causas profundas de la putrefacción y encontrar formas de frenar su avance antes de que consuma los bosques.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="As a Cenarion Circle brother, Terenthis represents the front line against the unnatural corruption spilling from Teldrassil into the mainland.",["race:NightElf"]="Terenthis exemplifies the kaldorei commitment to purifying their sacred lands from lingering fel taint and protecting innocent forest life."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Terenthis is a night elf druid affiliated with the Cenarion Circle, currently residing in the harbor town of Auberdine in Darkshore.",["al"]={"terenthis lore","who is terenthis","terenthis auberdine"},["q"]="Who is Terenthis?"},{["a"]="He was dispatched to investigate how widely Fel Moss and magical corruption have spread from Teldrassil into Darkshore, seeking a way to put an end to the blight.",["al"]={"what is terenthis doing","terenthis purpose","why is terenthis here"},["q"]="Why is Terenthis in Auberdine?"},{["a"]="The bear, Grimclaw, sought out Terenthis in Auberdine for help after his master, the druid Volcor, was attacked and wounded by hostile furbolgs.",["al"]={"terenthis bear","grimclaw","why is there a bear in auberdine"},["q"]="What is the bear beside Terenthis doing there?"},{["a"]="Terenthis is a member of the Cenarion Circle, the druidic order dedicated to preserving balance and safeguarding nature across Kalimdor.",["al"]={"terenthis faction","is terenthis cenarion circle"},["q"]="What organization does Terenthis belong to?"},{["a"]="He is primarily concerned with Fel Moss corruption affecting the regional wildlife, as well as the rising hostility of local furbolg tribes that threaten travelers and druids alike.",["al"]={"darkshore corruption","fel moss threat","terenthis concerns"},["q"]="What threats is Terenthis most concerned with?"},{["a"]="Yes. He directs adventurers to assess corrupting threats along the coast, coordinate with fellow druids like Thundris Windweaver, and mount a rescue for Volcor.",["al"]={"terenthis quests","what does terenthis want"},["q"]="Does Terenthis offer any tasks to adventurers?"}},["kw"]={"auberdine","cenarion circle","darkshore","fel moss","furbolg","grimclaw","terenthis","volcor"},["n"]="Terenthis",["s"]="Terenthis is a night elf druid stationed in the coastal settlement of Auberdine. Representing the Cenarion Circle, he is investigating the alarming corruption spreading through Darkshore and Teldrassil. He enlists capable travelers to gauge rising threats along the coast and assist local allies trapped by corrupted wildlife.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Sent to Auberdine by the Cenarion Circle, Terenthis focuses on tracking the spread of Fel Moss and other corruptive forces seeping into Darkshore from Teldrassil. The night elves view this creeping blight with immense concern, fearing the wild balance of northern Kalimdor may fracture completely if left unchecked. Terenthis works to uncover the root causes of the rot and devise ways to halt its advance before it consumes the forests.",["t"]="Investigating the Taint"},{["b"]="Terenthis also acts as a liaison for dire emergencies in the field. When the loyal bear Grimclaw arrives in Auberdine wounded and alone, Terenthis recognizes that the creature's master, the druid Volcor, has run into grave trouble. Lacking the ability to leave his post, Terenthis directs passing adventurers into the wilderness to find Volcor, who has been ambushed and pinned down by aggressive furbolg tribes.",["t"]="A Plea from Grimclaw"}}}}}
t["npc:theocritus"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="10,405,19.606.0,24.626.0,18.242.0,33.251.0,35.236.0,25.225.0,51.253.0,35.213.0",["h"]="8747dd",["n"]="Theocritus",["s"]="Theocritus. El archimago Theocritus es un excéntrico hechicero humano que reside en lo alto de la Torre de Azora, en el este del Bosque de Elwynn. Anteriormente vinculado al Kirin Tor de Dalaran, ahora vive de forma independiente, rodeado de sirvientes y dispositivos mágicos de clarividencia. Desde su elevado sagrario, Theocritus orienta sus talentos arcanos a vigilar el reino y combatir a su oscuro rival, el mago renegado Morganth. Antaño miembro del prestigioso Kirin Tor de Dalaran, el archimago Theocritus decidió establecer un bastión independiente muy al sur, en el reino de Ventormenta. Se asentó en la prominente Torre de Azora, situada cerca del camino oriental hacia Crestagrana. Theocritus es conocido por sus excéntricas costumbres y su cómodo estilo de vida, contando con un nutrido servicio doméstico que incluye a numerosos asistentes gnomos y a su propio pañero particular, Morley Eberlein. Aunque se mantiene en gran medida al margen de las preocupaciones mundanas de los aldeanos locales, su presencia sirve como un baluarte mágico fundamental en el este de Elwynn.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Mage"]="Theocritus represents the life of a wizard who operates outside Dalaran's strict hierarchy, demonstrating how solitary masters set up sanctums and conduct long-distance scrying.",["faction:Alliance"]="Though eccentric and aloof, Theocritus uses his arcane vision and resources to actively defend eastern Elwynn and Redridge from rogue spellcasters.",["race:Human"]="The conflict between Theocritus and Morganth mirrors the dual paths of human sorcery: disciplined scholarship dedicated to defense versus corruption and dark ambition."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Archmage Theocritus is a former Kirin Tor wizard who makes his home in the Tower of Azora in eastern Elwynn Forest. He lives an eccentric, somewhat isolated life, focusing his arcane craft on safeguarding the region from dark magical threats.",["al"]={"theocritus lore","who is the mage in the tower","tower of azora mage"},["q"]="Who is Theocritus?"},{["a"]="While he once operated within the Kirin Tor alongside peers like Archmage Karlain, Theocritus chose to become an independent practitioner. He relocated to Elwynn Forest to pursue his own studies and maintain his personal sanctum at the Tower of Azora.",["al"]={"is theocritus kirin tor","why is theocritus in elwynn","theocritus dalaran"},["q"]="Why did Theocritus leave Dalaran?"},{["a"]="His chief rival is Morganth, a fallen human mage who has taken up dark magic in the Tower of Ilgalar across the border in Redridge. Theocritus sees Morganth as both an offensive personal foe and a dire threat to the safety of Stormwind.",["al"]={"theocritus enemy","who is morganth","theocritus rival"},["q"]="Who is Theocritus fighting against?"},{["a"]="The Eye of Azora is a powerful scrying apparatus developed and housed by Theocritus atop his tower. He uses it to magically peer into distant lands, track threats, and even attempt to read the thoughts of his rival, Morganth.",["al"]={"eye of azora lore","how does theocritus spy","theocritus crystal ball"},["q"]="What is the Eye of Azora?"},{["a"]="The Shadowhide gnolls serve Morganth and wear enchanted pendants tied to their master. Theocritus studies these trinkets to learn how their magical link operates, hoping to broadcast an arcane attack through the network to paralyze the gnolls in battle.",["al"]={"gnoll pendants theocritus","theocritus retrieval","why collect gnoll pendants"},["q"]="Why does Theocritus want Shadowhide gnoll pendants?"},{["a"]="Theocritus surrounds himself with an unusual household, including an entire retinue of gnomish servants who see to his daily affairs, as well as a personal clothier named Morley Eberlein who tends to his wardrobe.",["al"]={"tower of azora staff","who lives in tower of azora","theocritus servants"},["q"]="Who serves Theocritus in his tower?"}},["kw"]={"archmage","elwynn forest","eye of azora","karlain","morganth","morley eberlein","shadowhide","theocritus","tower of azora"},["n"]="Theocritus",["s"]="Archmage Theocritus is an eccentric human wizard who resides at the peak of the Tower of Azora in eastern Elwynn Forest. Formerly affiliated with the Kirin Tor of Dalaran, he now lives independently, surrounded by servants and magical scrying devices. From his high sanctum, Theocritus directs his arcane talents toward keeping watch over the kingdom and combating his dark rival, the rogue mage Morganth.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Once a member of Dalaran's prestigious Kirin Tor, Archmage Theocritus chose to establish an independent stronghold far to the south in the kingdom of Stormwind. He settled in the prominent Tower of Azora, situated near the eastern road to Redridge. Theocritus is known for his eccentric habits and comfortable lifestyle, employing an extensive household staff that includes numerous gnomish attendants and his own dedicated clothier, Morley Eberlein. Though he keeps himself largely detached from the mundane concerns of local villagers, his presence serves as a critical magical bulwark in eastern Elwynn.",["t"]="Master of the Tower"},{["b"]="Theocritus's greatest ongoing concern is the fallen mage Morganth, a dangerous warlock operating from the Tower of Ilgalar in the nearby Redridge Mountains. Viewing Morganth both as a personal nemesis and a severe peril to Stormwind, Theocritus has dedicated months of arcane research to undermining him. Through scrying artifacts like the Eye of Azora, Theocritus monitors the villain's actions and delves into his thoughts. He also works to turn Morganth's own creations against him, studying the magical pendants carried by the Shadowhide gnolls in hopes of transmitting an arcane pulse that can immobilize the entire pack.",["t"]="The War Against Morganth"}}}}}
t["npc:thotar"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="6,374,22.474.0,16.459.0,14.165.0,26.116.0,34.224.0,28.209.0,45.226.0,49.228.0",["h"]="5968f6",["n"]="Thotar",["s"]="Thotar. Thotar es un experimentado instructor de cazadores orco apostado en el asentamiento de Cerrotajo, en Durotar. Guía a los futuros exploradores y tiradores de la Horda en las antiguas tradiciones del rastreo, la arquería y el vínculo con las bestias salvajes. Para los jóvenes orcos y trols que dan sus primeros pasos fuera del Valle de los Retos, él proporciona los ritos fundamentales necesarios para dominar la escarpada fauna de Kalimdor. Ubicado dentro del enclave fortificado de Cerrotajo, Thotar ejerce de veterano instructor para los tiradores de la Horda. Mientras que los nuevos reclutas aprenden los conceptos más básicos en el Valle de los Retos, a Thotar le corresponde guiar a los cazadores cuando se enfrentan a la naturaleza depredadora y más hostil de Durotar. Basándose en tradiciones transmitidas a lo largo de incontables generaciones de orcos, no solo enseña puntería, sino también el profundo respeto requerido para convivir con las criaturas más letales de Kalimdor y dirigirlas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Hunter"]="Thotar represents a key milestone for young Horde hunters, teaching the vital rites of beast taming and wilderness mastery once novices step out of the starter valleys.",["faction:Horde"]="As a frontline trainer in Razor Hill, Thotar ensures that scouts and marksmen patrolling Durotar's borders are disciplined, sharp-eyed, and well-bonded with combat beasts.",["race:Orc"]="Thotar preserves and passes down traditional orcish hunting customs, ensuring that life on Kalimdor remains anchored in deep ancestral respect for tracking and beast companionship.",["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear hunters setting out from Sen'jin Village, Thotar offers vital instruction that blends ancestral Horde survival skills with the predatory challenges of Durotar."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Thotar is a veteran orc hunter trainer stationed in Razor Hill in Durotar. He educates young hunters in traditional wilderness lore, marksmanship, and animal taming.",["al"]={"who is thotar","thotar lore","what does thotar do"},["q"]="Who is Thotar?"},{["a"]="He is located in the Horde settlement of Razor Hill, situated in central Durotar just north of the Valley of Trials.",["al"]={"thotar location","where is thotar","find thotar"},["q"]="Where can Thotar be found?"},{["a"]="Thotar teaches the ancient survival and tracking traditions passed down through generations of orcs. He emphasizes weapon mastery, wilderness survival, and learning to bond with animal companions through patience and ritual.",["al"]={"what does thotar teach","hunter traditions","thotar training"},["q"]="What traditions does Thotar teach?"},{["a"]="While he is an orc steeped in his people's ways, Thotar instructs any hunter aligned with the Horde who arrives in Razor Hill, regularly mentoring Darkspear trolls and wandering tauren passing through Durotar.",["al"]={"can trolls train with thotar","thotar tauren","who does thotar train"},["q"]="Does Thotar only train orcs?"},{["a"]="Thotar directs novice hunters on the rites of 'Taming the Beast,' tasking them with tracking down native Durotar wildlife—such as boars, surf crawlers, and scorpids—and using a taming rod to earn their trust and obedience.",["al"]={"thotar quests","taming the beast thotar","what does thotar send you to do"},["q"]="What tasks does Thotar give to young hunters?"},{["a"]="For Horde hunters, a beast companion is a vital partner on the battlefield and in the wild. Thotar teaches that properly bonding with a beast ensures mutual survival, transforming raw predators into loyal defenders of the Horde.",["al"]={"why tame beasts","hunter pet lore","purpose of beast taming"},["q"]="Why is beast taming so important in his training?"}},["kw"]={"durotar","hunter","hunter trainer","kaplak","orc","razor hill","taming the beast","thotar"},["n"]="Thotar",["s"]="Thotar is a seasoned orc hunter trainer stationed in the settlement of Razor Hill in Durotar. He guides aspiring Horde scouts and marksmen in the ancient traditions of tracking, archery, and bonding with wild beasts. For young orcs and trolls taking their first steps outside the Valley of Trials, he provides the foundational rites needed to master Kalimdor's rugged fauna.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Perched within the fortified hub of Razor Hill, Thotar serves as a veteran instructor for marksmen of the Horde. While new recruits learn the very basics in the Valley of Trials, it falls to Thotar to guide hunters as they face the harsher predatory wilderness of Durotar. Drawing upon traditions passed down through countless generations of orcs, he teaches not only marksmanship, but the deeper respect required to live alongside and direct Kalimdor's deadliest creatures.",["t"]="A Mentor in Razor Hill"},{["b"]="Thotar plays a crucial role in introducing young hunters to the ancient art of beast taming. Through a sequence of trials, he sends novices into the arid canyons to pacify and commune with native beasts, such as venomous scorpid, armored surf crawlers, and cunning boars. By guiding these young scouts through the sacred rites of taming, Thotar ensures the Horde's trackers build a loyal bond with nature rather than merely attempting to dominate it by force.",["t"]="Taming the Wilds"}}}}}
t["npc:thrall"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="6,309,20.582.0,26.515.0,21.637.0,14.279.0,35.276.0,52.288.0,36.165.0,52.297.0,49.333.0",["h"]="ad30ed",["n"]="Thrall",["s"]="Thrall. Thrall es el Jefe de Guerra de la Horda y el gobernante de Durotar, y celebra audiencia desde el Valle de la Sabiduría en Orgrimmar. Antaño esclavo de los humanos y criado para ser gladiador de arena, rompió las cadenas de su pueblo, redescubrió sus antiguas tradiciones chamánicas y lo guio a través del Mare Magnum para construir un nuevo hogar. Nacido como Go'el, hijo del caudillo de los Lobo Gélido Durotan y de Draka, Thrall quedó huérfano siendo un bebé cuando sus padres fueron asesinados por los sicarios de Gul'dan. Fue descubierto por el comandante humano Aedelas Lodonegro, quien lo llamó «Thrall» —que significa esclavo— y lo crio en el Castillo de Durnholde como luchador de arena con formación en tácticas humanas. Ayudado por su hermana de acogida Taretha Foxton, Thrall acabó escapando de sus captores. Guiado por el exiliado del Clan Lobo Gélido Drek'Thar, dejó a un lado la corrupción demoníaca para dominar a los espíritus elementales, convirtiéndose en el primero de una nueva generación de chamanes orcos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Shaman"]="Thrall is revered as the first new orcish shaman in a generation, having restored the sacred communion between his people and the elemental spirits after decades of demonic corruption.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance leaders view Thrall as a dangerous yet pragmatic leader whose disciplined Horde is vastly preferable to the bloodthirsty conquerors of the First and Second Wars.",["faction:Horde"]="Thrall is your supreme commander and Warchief, having led the Horde out of enslavement and ruin to claim an honorable future on Kalimdor.",["race:Orc"]="To the orcs, Thrall is a living savior who broke the lethargy of the human internment camps and returned the race to its ancestral honor."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Thrall is the Warchief of the Horde and the leader of the orcish people. Born Go'el of the Frostwolf clan, he was raised as an enslaved gladiator by humans before breaking free, learning the shamanic arts, and leading the orcs to Kalimdor to found their new capital of Orgrimmar.",["al"]={"who is the warchief","thrall backstory","who is thrall"},["q"]="Who is Thrall?"},{["a"]="His birth name is Go'el, given by his parents Durotan and Draka. His human captor, Aedelas Blackmoore, named him 'Thrall'—an old human word meaning slave. Thrall retained the name as a reminder of where he came from and the oppression his people swore never to endure again.",["al"]={"why is he called thrall","what does thrall mean","thrall real name"},["q"]="Where does Thrall's name come from?"},{["a"]="Thrall wears the black plate armor and wields the Doomhammer passed to him by Orgrim Doomhammer, the former Warchief. Upon receiving a mortal wound during the liberation of the internment camps, Orgrim bestowed both the weapon and the mantle of Warchief upon Thrall with his dying breath.",["al"]={"doomhammer","thrall weapon","black armor"},["q"]="Why does Thrall wear black armor and carry a hammer?"},{["a"]="Thrall resides inside the Valley of Wisdom within Orgrimmar, the Horde capital in Durotar. He stands inside Grommash Hold accompanied by his bodyguards and advisers.",["al"]={"where is thrall","thrall location","thrall room"},["q"]="Where can I find Thrall in the game?"},{["a"]="Thrall and Lady Jaina Proudmoore forged a mutual respect and pact of cooperation while fighting alongside each other during the Third War at Mount Hyjal. Though their respective factions remain deeply distrustful, the two leaders strive to preserve a fragile peace between Orgrimmar and Theramore.",["al"]={"thrall and jaina","jaina alliance","peace with theramore"},["q"]="What is Thrall's relationship with Jaina Proudmoore?"},{["a"]="While cautious of the undead, Thrall recognized the desperate plight of Sylvanas Windrunner's Forsaken, who had freed themselves from the Lich King's control. Aided by the diplomatic urging of the tauren, who believe the Forsaken can be redeemed, Thrall granted them membership to secure a strategic foothold in the Eastern Kingdoms.",["al"]={"why are undead in horde","forsaken alliance","sylvanas horde entry"},["q"]="Why did Thrall allow the Forsaken into the Horde?"}},["kw"]={"blackmoore","doomhammer","durotar","go'el","orgrimmar","shaman","thrall","warchief"},["n"]="Thrall",["s"]="Thrall is the Warchief of the Horde and the ruler of Durotar, holding court from the Valley of Wisdom in Orgrimmar. Once a human slave raised to be an arena gladiator, he broke the chains of his people, rediscovered their ancient shamanic traditions, and led them across the Great Sea to build a new homeland.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Born Go'el, the son of Frostwolf chieftain Durotan and Draka, Thrall was orphaned as an infant when his parents were murdered by Gul'dan's assassins. He was discovered by human commander Aedelas Blackmoore, who named him 'Thrall'—meaning slave—and raised him at Durnholde Keep as an arena fighter with an education in human tactics. Aided by his foster sister Taretha Foxton, Thrall eventually escaped his captors. Guided by the Frostwolf exile Drek'Thar, he cast aside demonic corruption to master the elemental spirits, becoming the first of a new generation of orcish shaman.",["t"]="From Slave to Shaman"},{["b"]="Thrall joined forces with the legendary Orgrim Doomhammer to liberate the lethargic orcs languishing in Alliance internment camps after the Second War. When Doomhammer fell in battle, he bestowed his black plate armor and mighty warhammer upon Thrall, naming him the new Warchief. Following prophetic visions from the mysterious Prophet Medivh, Thrall led his people to commandeer human ships and sail across the Great Sea to the forgotten continent of Kalimdor, escaping the doom falling upon the Eastern Kingdoms.",["t"]="The Mantle of the Warchief"},{["b"]="In Kalimdor, Thrall reshaped the Horde from a warmongering engine into an alliance of survival and honor. He rescued the Darkspear trolls led by Vol'jin and allied with Cairne Bloodhoof's tauren before leading the coalition alongside human and night elf forces to defeat the Burning Legion atop Mount Hyjal. Afterward, Thrall founded the nation of Durotar and its capital Orgrimmar, named after his father and mentor. Despite maintaining an uneasy peace with Jaina Proudmoore's Theramore, Thrall now balances the defense of his fragile nation with controversial alliances, such as admitting the Forsaken of Lordaeron into the Horde fold.",["t"]="Forging the New Horde"}}}}}
